<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e078ec11-e461-4020-880c-e48ff2143e35> <https://schema.org/description> "The Arkansas Center for Biodiversity Collections is an active group of research and teaching collections within the Department of Biological Sciences at Arkansas State University. The ACBC includes collections of aquatic macroinvertebrates, bivalves, mammals, reptiles and amphibians, fish, insects, and birds. There is a heavy regional focus within Arkansas, with specific geographic areas of interest being the Ozark Plateaus region, Crowley’s Ridge, and the Mississippi Alluvial Plain. " .
