<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b4ca487f-ab13-4f7d-9b64-e7b3707197db> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b4ca487f-ab13-4f7d-9b64-e7b3707197db> <https://schema.org/name> "Administration des ponts et chaussées Luxembourg" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b4ca487f-ab13-4f7d-9b64-e7b3707197db> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "LU:PCH" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b4ca487f-ab13-4f7d-9b64-e7b3707197db> <https://schema.org/description> "The ‘Administration des ponts et chaussées’ is a public administration body under the authority of the Ministry of Mobility and Public Works in Luxembourg. The Administration is responsible, within the limits set by laws and regulations, for civil engineering works on behalf of the State. In addition to the Directorate, the Administration includes eleven divisions and eleven regional offices. Other key units include the Airport Service, the Motorway Traffic Control and Information Service (CITA), the Motorway Maintenance and Emergency Response Centre, the Electromechanical Service and the Tree Pruning Team. The ‘Administration des ponts et chaussées’ manages a stock of around 65,000 trees, comprising avenues, rows of trees, parkland and solitary trees. However, the majority of this inventory consists of street trees, which stand in rows or avenues along our national road network. We are committed to preserving and maintaining our native avenues, whilst also seeking to establish new plantings by introducing so-called ‘climate trees’, in order to determine which tree species and varieties will thrive in the future and cope with current and future climatic conditions in the context of climate change." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b4ca487f-ab13-4f7d-9b64-e7b3707197db> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q56305512> .
