<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/54ece787-14fb-4478-b923-7b5518578f04> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/54ece787-14fb-4478-b923-7b5518578f04> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/54ece787-14fb-4478-b923-7b5518578f04> <https://schema.org/name> "Khaldunia College of Pharmacy Herbarium" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/54ece787-14fb-4478-b923-7b5518578f04> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "KITAAS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/54ece787-14fb-4478-b923-7b5518578f04> <https://schema.org/description> "The Khaldunia College of Pharmacy Herbarium is an academic and research-oriented botanical repository established to support education, research, and documentation in the fields of Pharmacognosy, Botany, and Natural Product Sciences. It serves as a systematic collection of preserved plant specimens, primarily focusing on medicinal and economically important flora. The herbarium is designed to facilitate practical learning for Pharm.D students by enabling hands-on identification, classification, and study of plant materials used in traditional and modern medicine. Each specimen is carefully collected, pressed, dried, mounted, and labeled with essential taxonomic and ethnopharmacological information, including scientific name, family, local name, habitat, and medicinal uses. In addition to its educational role, the herbarium contributes to biodiversity conservation and the documentation of indigenous plant knowledge. It aims to develop into a digital herbarium in the future, integrating modern tools for global accessibility and collaboration with international botanical databases. Through this initiative, Khaldunia College of Pharmacy is committed to promoting research excellence, preserving plant heritage, and strengthening the scientific foundation of herbal medicine in Pakistan." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/54ece787-14fb-4478-b923-7b5518578f04> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(74.211007 31.45332)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/54ece787-14fb-4478-b923-7b5518578f04> <https://schema.org/logo> <https://kitaas.edu.pk/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/kitaas-1-1.png> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/141305b6-2c66-4bbb-a1fb-a0eafd471be0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
