<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4716fb53-997a-4b8b-bc88-32c31fea2a91> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4716fb53-997a-4b8b-bc88-32c31fea2a91> <https://schema.org/name> "Petaluma Wildlife Museum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4716fb53-997a-4b8b-bc88-32c31fea2a91> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "PWM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4716fb53-997a-4b8b-bc88-32c31fea2a91> <https://schema.org/description> "Founded in 1992, the Petaluma Wildlife Museum (PWM) has been the home of an extensive taxidermy collection and small animal zoo. It is the first and only high school student-run natural history museum in the nation. The museum collection itself has been built through community donations, primarily through the inheritance of the Codding Museum of Natural History in Santa Rosa taxidermy collection. The species representation has primarily focused on North American and African species. " .
