<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/00f93b00-a375-4c3b-b6a4-119f89b1b78d> <https://schema.org/description> "The Natural Sciences Museum is a relatively new independent natural history museum located in at 149 Holme Lane, Sheffield S6 4JR, and opened to the public on 13 August 2022. The museum is focused chiefly on palaeontological specimens. It has 12,000 specimens, a CT-scanner, a public preparation lab, and a private conservation lab. " .
