<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/146f6496-7204-49f1-a9cd-ede713d10b47> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/146f6496-7204-49f1-a9cd-ede713d10b47> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/146f6496-7204-49f1-a9cd-ede713d10b47> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/146f6496-7204-49f1-a9cd-ede713d10b47> <https://schema.org/name> "Museu de la Universitat de València d’Història Natural (MUVHN)" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/146f6496-7204-49f1-a9cd-ede713d10b47> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "MUVHN" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/146f6496-7204-49f1-a9cd-ede713d10b47> <https://schema.org/description> "The MUVHN is the natural history museum of the University of Valencia (Spain). It houses and manages scientific collections of high historical and research value, including zoological, paleontological and mineralogical material. The entomological collection is one of its largest and most significant holdings, partly exhibited in the museum but mainly preserved in storage facilities under appropriate conditions. These collections are available for consultation by national and international researchers upon request. The MUVHN’s mission is to conserve, document, digitize and disseminate the natural heritage of the Universitat de València and associated institutions, supporting both scientific research and public engagement. The museum is also actively involved in collaborative projects on biodiversity, taxonomy and conservation, contributing data and expertise to the scientific community." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/146f6496-7204-49f1-a9cd-ede713d10b47> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-0.420919 39.507099)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

