<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6e7d1ef1-e06f-4437-85d3-f9c62e65d14a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6e7d1ef1-e06f-4437-85d3-f9c62e65d14a> <https://schema.org/name> "M.M. Hryshko National Botanical Garden of the National Academy of Sciences of Ukraine" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6e7d1ef1-e06f-4437-85d3-f9c62e65d14a> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "HNBG" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6e7d1ef1-e06f-4437-85d3-f9c62e65d14a> <https://schema.org/description> "The M. M. Hryshko National Botanical Garden of the National Academy of Sciences of Ukraine in Kyiv is one of Eastern Europe’s largest botanical gardens, founded in 1936 and named after the renowned botanist Mykola Mykolayovych Hryshko. Covering over 130 hectares, it features extensive plant collections from around the world, including unique thematic areas such as the “Flora of Ukraine,” exotic and tropical greenhouses, aromatic and medicinal plants, and rare endangered species. The garden serves as a leading center for botanical research, conservation, environmental education, and recreation, attracting scientists, students, and visitors from across the globe." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6e7d1ef1-e06f-4437-85d3-f9c62e65d14a> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(30.557969 50.415476)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/917c3b95-ec96-40bd-a18d-d4f88e41f94f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
