<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7492b93f-9175-480f-8e90-32c1c2b633fa> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated Mar 2015. The Luis Diego Gomez Herbarium is located at the Las Cruces Biological Station (8° 47' 7'' N, 82° 57' 32'' W), one of three field stations owned and operated by the Organization for Tropical Studies (OTS; www.ots.cr) in Costa Rica. This is a young herbarium (inaugurated 2006) but a comprehensive collection of the regional flora of southern Costa Rica is well underway, and all specimens are scanned and uploaded to the OTS plant database website (www.ots.cr/plantdatabase). The collecting is only ~1,400 km2 but spans an elevational gradient of 300 - 3200 m and a rainfall range from 1.5 - 5 m (see website for a map of collecting range). Flora of southern Costa Rica. Vascular plants" .
