<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8b760d1f-f4a7-4ee0-81e6-5a5c344124a4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8b760d1f-f4a7-4ee0-81e6-5a5c344124a4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8b760d1f-f4a7-4ee0-81e6-5a5c344124a4> <https://schema.org/name> "Inverness Museum & Art Gallery" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8b760d1f-f4a7-4ee0-81e6-5a5c344124a4> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "IMVMG" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8b760d1f-f4a7-4ee0-81e6-5a5c344124a4> <https://schema.org/description> "Inverness Museum & Art Gallery’s roots go back to 1825 with the formation of the Northern Institute – a society in Inverness for the promotion of science, literature and the history of Scotland and the Highlands. The Northern Institute flourished in its early years and established a museum based on collections assembled by members between 1825 and 1834. This establishment would struggle in later years from want of a permanent home, and when the Northern Institute disbanded in 1873. The formation of the Inverness Scientific Society and Field Club in 1875 led to considerable strengthening of the museum’s collections of natural history, especially botany, geology and zoology, the collections of archaeology and historical Highland artefacts also grew. , The Natural Sciences collections held by Inverness Museum & Art Gallery comprise approximately 35,000 specimens, subdivided into mineralogy, palaeontology, invertebrate zoology, vertebrate zoology and botany. , The mineralogical collections consist of appr.. The majority of specimens are from the Highlands, Scotland, including Inverness-shire, Ross-shire, Sutherland and Caithness. There is wider Scottish material and a limited amount of foreign material." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8b760d1f-f4a7-4ee0-81e6-5a5c344124a4> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-4.226006 57.477)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

