<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b9420488-db21-47d7-ad26-31c10c1000d1> <https://schema.org/description> "Hengchun Research Center was founded in 1902 when Japanese rule era under the auspices of the Products Bureau of Taiwan Governor General’s Office. The bureau established a seed orchard in each of its 4 nurseries: Gueizihjiao, Gangkou Village, Chulaoshu (Lideh), and Gaoshifo; and set up an office at Gueizihjiao. Around the office there were many specimen gardens for collecting tropical economic plants, which was the forerunner of today's “Hengchun Tropical Botanic Garden”. Vascular plants, especially of tropical and subtropical areas." .
