<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e7a0f3c0-266b-41c7-834d-efdee56ec2c6> <https://schema.org/name> "Universidade Santa Cecilia-UNISANTA" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e7a0f3c0-266b-41c7-834d-efdee56ec2c6> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "HUSC" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e7a0f3c0-266b-41c7-834d-efdee56ec2c6> <https://schema.org/description> "Entered Feb 2012 .Our main goal is to provide the community with service on issues concerning an accurate identification of the plants, as well as preserve the testimony of scientific studies carried out by undergarduate and and post-graduate students in the areas of ecology, taxonomy, phytotheraphy and pharmacognosy.; Our main area of study is the Atlantic forest biome in the state of São Paulo's coastal region, Brazil, in the following ecosystems: mangrove, restinga (coastal plain forest), dense rainforest. This collection represents the flora of Bertioga's restinga (Parque Estadual da Restinga de Bertioga, Portuguese for Bertioga's Restinga State Park). It also contains mosses and hepatics from the state of São Paulo; algae from state of São Paulo's coastal region, the flora from Santos' Botanical Garden, and native and exotic medicinal plants used by the population in Baixada Santista." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e7a0f3c0-266b-41c7-834d-efdee56ec2c6> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-46.3219 -23.963)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

