<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3994bb92-2385-4699-a621-6a3511b0c45d> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated Dec 2013. M. Guiry retired in 2009, and the algal materials (those of Guiry and Mairin De Valera) are now in the Ryan Institute, National University of Ireland Galway. The small flowering plant herbarium is still at the Botany & Plant Science discipline of the School of Natural Sciences. The code \"GALW\" applies to both collections. The algal herbarium has 15,500 numbered specimens; the flowering plants, mosses and lichen herbarium comprise 2,000- 3,000 specimens, of which the vascular plant collection is the greatest and is currently the only numbered collection. Most of the lichen collection was re-housed in DBN in 2001. Marine algae, especially Rhodophyta; vascular plants, mosses and lichens of Ireland." .
