<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/55343ef1-fbb4-4cf2-8e62-ff7ebe1329e8> <https://schema.org/description> "Scotland's oldest independent museum, opened in 1843 to house collections dating from 1836. The palaeontology collection and its archive is Recognised as nationally important, containing Type specimens for Devonian fish, and Permian and Triassic reptiles. The wider collection illustrates the development and history of life in Moray, Scotland, Britain and connections with the wider world." .
