<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/58f45a9c-b36b-41c0-9ad2-b8cf70a16b77> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated Sep 2015 (staff, collection total). The Herbarium of V. N. Karazin Kharkiv National University was founded in 1825, now preserves ca. 300 000 specimens of plants, fungi and lichens, including mycological and lichenological exsiccates. Current acronym is CWU, old acronym CWB is no longer used. CWU consists of three sub-repositories: 1) Department of Botany (CWU); 3) Department of Mycology and Plant Resistance (CWU-MYC); 1) Kharkiv Botanical Garden (CWB). Specialty: Ukraine, Russia (European part, Far East), Europe (Czech Republic, Slovak vachchyna, Mediterranean countries), Caucasus, Kazakhstan, Central Asia, Africa, Australia, Central in America (Nicaragua, Cuba). Western, central, and eastern Europe." .
