<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c810c9fd-d365-4882-8c40-51b137525ce4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c810c9fd-d365-4882-8c40-51b137525ce4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c810c9fd-d365-4882-8c40-51b137525ce4> <https://schema.org/name> "Royal Holloway College, University of London" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c810c9fd-d365-4882-8c40-51b137525ce4> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "RHUL" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c810c9fd-d365-4882-8c40-51b137525ce4> <https://schema.org/description> "Royal Holloway is formed from two pioneering colleges (Bedford College and Royal Holloway) for the education of women in the 19th century. The two colleges merged in 1985. The combined natural history collections date back to the 19th century and encorporate material collected for teaching and research within the former Departments of zoology, botany, physiology, geography, and geology. The collections are presently housed within the School of Life Sciences and the Environment which is made up of the Departments of Biological Sciences, Psychology, Geography, and Earth Sciences and are located in two adjacent buildings (Bourne and Wolfson). The college also contains an arboretum, a 3.5 acre garden of unusual and rare trees planted in the early 1950's as part of the University of London's Botanical Supply Unit" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c810c9fd-d365-4882-8c40-51b137525ce4> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1202039> .
