<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/0d75b29a-ee14-4ea0-9412-7d02a87f32e8> <https://schema.org/description> "In the five rooms of exhibits and collections saved in Sponges, Corals, Mollusks, Arachnids, Insects, Crustaceans, Fish, Amphibians, Reptiles, Birds, Mammals. Today, the museum more than 170 thousand items, of which about 10 thousand form the exhibition. The funds, in turn, are as follows: invertebrates - 2123 units, malaсological - 44297 units, entomological - 91898 units, ichthyological - 688 units, amphibians - 545 units, reptiles - 364 units, ornithological - 5191 units, oological fund - 841 units, mammals - 2858 units, osteological fund - 490 units, Collection E.-F. Germar - 4258 units, Collection of N.I. Srebrodolska - 358 units, Collection F.I. Strautman - 1108 units, a Collection of O. Schtodinger - 2119 units, Collection A. Ulyanowski - 5000 units, Collection S.K. Pietrusky - 7460 units. The museum preserves more than 130 type specimens of animals, that is, those which were first discovered and described to science. They come from the Ukraine, Russia, Poland, Brazil, India, Mexico, Australia, Eastern and Central Africa, the countries of Central Europe." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/0e919a55-08d3-4bd2-aec1-200858fafd92> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/0e919a55-08d3-4bd2-aec1-200858fafd92> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/0e919a55-08d3-4bd2-aec1-200858fafd92> <https://schema.org/name> "Naturalis Biodiversity Center" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/0e919a55-08d3-4bd2-aec1-200858fafd92> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "Naturalis" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/0e919a55-08d3-4bd2-aec1-200858fafd92> <https://schema.org/description> "The beginnings of Naturalis Biodiversity Center go back to the creation of the 'Rijksmuseum van Natuurlijke Historie' (acronym RMNH, National Museum of Natural History) by Dutch King William I on August 9, 1820. In 1878, the geological and mineralogical collections of the museum were split off into a separate museum, the 'Rijksmuseum van Geologie en Mineralogie' (acronym RGM). RGM remained distinct until the merger with the 'Rijksmuseum van Natuurlijke Historie' (RMNH) in 1984, to form the 'Nationaal Natuurhistorisch Museum' (NNM) or National Museum of Natural History, later renamed 'Naturalis'. In 2010 Naturalis was further combined with the Zoological Museum Amsterdam (ZMA) of the University of Amsterdam, and the Dutch National Herbaria at the universities of Leiden, Utrecht, Amsterdam and Wageningen, to form the 'Nederlands Centrum voor Biodiversiteit' (NCB). In 2012 its name became the Naturalis Biodiversity Center. Worldwide." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/0e919a55-08d3-4bd2-aec1-200858fafd92> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q641676> .
