<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/23551915-cca0-4096-a4be-5cc38cc99578> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/23551915-cca0-4096-a4be-5cc38cc99578> <https://schema.org/name> "Gros Morne National Park" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/23551915-cca0-4096-a4be-5cc38cc99578> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "GMNP" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/23551915-cca0-4096-a4be-5cc38cc99578> <https://schema.org/description> "Herbarium for Parks Canada, Western Newfoundland and Labrador Field Unit Specialty: Bryophytes; vascular plants; Gros Morne National Park, Torngat Mountains National Park, Red Bay National Historic Site, Port au Choix National Historic Site, L'Anse aux Meadows National Historic Site, and some general Newfoundland and Labrador collections. Specimens are organized in a single numbering system (no collection codes). Within the database everything can be sorted by taxonomic subdivisions, location, collector, etc. Also, temporarily the repository for the fungal collection of Foray Newfoundland and Labrador, which amounts to about 3,000 specimens representing 1,000 species.Inst. type: Federal government, Parks Canada|Additional Correspondents: Michael Burzynski, Michael.Burzynski@pc.gc.ca; Anne Marceau, Chief Park Interpreter, anne_marceau@pch.gc.ca|IH upload June 2010. Bryophytes; vascular plants; Gros Morne National Park, vascular plants of Port au Choix National Historic Site, Red Bay National Historic Site, L'Anse aux Meadows National Historic Site, and Torngat Mountains Nationsl Park" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/23551915-cca0-4096-a4be-5cc38cc99578> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-57.923462 49.589508)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

