<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/2749cf1e-60d9-4b03-9c71-3763632b8f78> <https://schema.org/name> "Museum of New Zealand Te Papa Tongarewa" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/2749cf1e-60d9-4b03-9c71-3763632b8f78> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "NMNZ" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/2749cf1e-60d9-4b03-9c71-3763632b8f78> <https://schema.org/description> "The Natural History Team at Te Papa, Aotearoa New Zealand's national museum, cares for comprehensive collections of marine and freshwater fishes, marine mammals, birds, reptiles, fossil vertebrates, molluscs, insects and plants. The Natural History collections have a broad geographical spread across the New Zealand region, and in some cases internationally, but with a central focus on the South Pacific region. There are approximately 1.2 million specimen lots in the Natural History collection. The Natural History collection consists of zoological and botany specimens; with an estimated 700,000 invertebrate lots and 120,000 vertebrate lots in the zoological collections, and an estimated 300,000 lots in the botany collections. Broad geographical spread across the New Zealand region, and in some cases internationally, but with a central focus on the South Pacific region. Comprehensive collections of marine and freshwater fishes, marine mammals, birds, reptiles, fossil vertebrates, molluscs, insects and plants." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/2749cf1e-60d9-4b03-9c71-3763632b8f78> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(174.781921 -41.290348)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
