<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/311d25be-7fef-4f7e-9eb1-daa30d61f2df> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/311d25be-7fef-4f7e-9eb1-daa30d61f2df> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/311d25be-7fef-4f7e-9eb1-daa30d61f2df> <https://schema.org/name> "North Carolina State University Insect Museum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/311d25be-7fef-4f7e-9eb1-daa30d61f2df> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "NCSU" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/311d25be-7fef-4f7e-9eb1-daa30d61f2df> <https://schema.org/description> "Our holdings are partitioned into four main collections (all specimens use the same numbering system and do not require collection codes): NC State University Insect Collection - the vast majority of our specimens are housed here in the research collection Genome Bank - our cold storage collection for specimens used in molecular analyses NC State University Teaching Collection - approximately 60 drawers of insects used in our insect systematics course (ENT 502) NC State University Outreach Collection - approximately 8 drawers used for outreach ~1,400,000 prepared specimens. Holdings of North Carolina insects and of Hemiptera are especially outstanding. The NCSU Insect Collection has several other outstanding research collections (mainly Lepidoptera, Acari, Anthophila (the bees), Diptera, Coleoptera, Heteroptera, Orthoptera, and Collembola) within it and associated assemblages of literature that are of international importance." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/35bb26b8-f1de-462c-b167-fd4edefe1f84> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/35bb26b8-f1de-462c-b167-fd4edefe1f84> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
