<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/44c2b14c-c62c-461f-b55c-84acc7944ccd> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated Nov 2011 (new permit requirements). A permit (PPQ588) is now required to import herbarium specimens (including our own return loans) from outside the US. Our permit number is PDEP-11-00268. This number should be written on the outside of the parcel and also on the shipping notice. A copy of our permit should be enclosed in the package. We can send an electronic file of the permit via email.; ; AHUC intercalated with DAV, but should still be cited as AHUC. Number of specimens cited for DAV includes AHUC and DAVH. DAV named John M. Tucker Herbarium in 1986; however the consolidated herbaria (DAV, AHUC, and DAVH) are now known as UC Davis Center for Plant Diversity, which has the acronym DAV. Library includes botanical libraries of B. Crampton, J. Major, L. C. Wheeler, and G. L. Webster. Worldwide, with emphasis on California and neotropics (especially Ecuador and Baja California); , Fagaceae, and , Ericaceae of New World; Euphorbiaceae; Poaceae; Solanaceae; weedy and poisonous species of Mediterranean-climate regions; range plants of California; alpine flora of western North America." .
