<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d2a27206-87ab-47ea-b5fc-d2e57054b688> <https://schema.org/description> "Based in San Francisco, the California Academy of Sciences is home to more than 100 research scientists and nearly 46 million scientific specimens from around the world. The Academy’s research collections include the Dudley Herbarium from Stanford University (DS, since recataloged as CASBOT-BC), the Indiana University fish collection (IU, recataloged as CASICH), the Stanford University fish collection (CASSU(ICH)), and the Stanford University herpetology collection (CASSUA, CASSUR). Worldwide, especially western North America and California. Anthropology, Botany, Entomology, Geology (Fossil), Herpetology, Invertebrate Zoology, Ichthyology, Mammalogy, Ornithology." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d2a27206-87ab-47ea-b5fc-d2e57054b688> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-122.466789 37.770241)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

