<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/fa252605-26f6-426c-9892-94d071c2c77f> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "K" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/fa252605-26f6-426c-9892-94d071c2c77f> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated Nov 2012 (staff updates). Kew founded as a government institution in 1841; Kew herbarium and library founded in 1852. Total of 7 million specimens, including approximately 350 000 types. Digitisation of specimens is underway. Specimens of original Wallich Herbarium (K-W) not sent on loan. K lichens, bryophytes, and algae transferred to BM. Library and Archives information at http://www.kew.org/library/index.html. Worldwide vascular plants and larger fungi, especially rich in types and collections from Africa, tropical Asia, and Australasia; emphasis on families of major economic importance." .
