<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/0360f257-7121-45f1-8947-14a3600e56af> <https://schema.org/description> "The Centre for Biodiversity Genomics (CBG) is the global leader in the field of DNA barcoding. It occupies a 50,000 ft2 facility on the University of Guelph campus in Guelph, Canada. Its unique research capacity reflects the coupling of one of Canada’s largest genomics platforms with a workforce that includes world-class expertise in biodiversity science, DNA sequencing, and informatics." .
