<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7daac953-eb01-4445-9a01-0e3ba1f33587> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7daac953-eb01-4445-9a01-0e3ba1f33587> <https://schema.org/name> "Culture Collection of Antimicrobial Resistant Microbes" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7daac953-eb01-4445-9a01-0e3ba1f33587> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "CCARM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7daac953-eb01-4445-9a01-0e3ba1f33587> <https://schema.org/description> "CCARM collects bacteria from human, animals, and environment, identify, assays MICs, characterize the resistant mechanism, stores, and distributes to researchers. In addition to these activities, CCARM provides various services and various information through homepage and publish bulletin. Since CCARM started in 1999, it has been members of Clinical Laboratory Standard Institute (CLSI), World Federation for Culture Collection (WFCC), and International Society for Biological and Environmental Repositories (ISBER)." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/846440c5-ce6c-4f67-943a-afad75eb8757> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/846440c5-ce6c-4f67-943a-afad75eb8757> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/846440c5-ce6c-4f67-943a-afad75eb8757> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/846440c5-ce6c-4f67-943a-afad75eb8757> <https://schema.org/name> "Ghent University" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/846440c5-ce6c-4f67-943a-afad75eb8757> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "UGENT" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/846440c5-ce6c-4f67-943a-afad75eb8757> <https://schema.org/description> "Ghent University is a top 100 university and one of the major universities in Belgium. Our 11 faculties offer more than 200 courses and conduct in-depth research within a wide range of scientific domains. Ghent University Global Campus is also the first European university in Songdo, South Korea." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/846440c5-ce6c-4f67-943a-afad75eb8757> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1137665> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/846440c5-ce6c-4f67-943a-afad75eb8757> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/00cv9y106> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/846440c5-ce6c-4f67-943a-afad75eb8757> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(3.72207 51.036461)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/846440c5-ce6c-4f67-943a-afad75eb8757> <https://schema.org/logo> <https://www.gum.gent/img/logo/logo_nl.svg> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/863b6bcc-4410-4b51-a2f0-a441dc340b7d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/863b6bcc-4410-4b51-a2f0-a441dc340b7d> <https://schema.org/name> "Korea Prostate Bank" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/863b6bcc-4410-4b51-a2f0-a441dc340b7d> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "KPB" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/863b6bcc-4410-4b51-a2f0-a441dc340b7d> <https://schema.org/description> "The Korea Prostate Bank was established October 2006 as part of the Korean National Research Resources Bank. We collect human prostate cancer specimens (frozen tissue, plasma, serum, gDNA) of prostate cancer patients. KPB also stores collection of images (CT, MRI, etc.) of the prostate." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/906faeb6-e566-4020-9937-365c91a8f123> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/906faeb6-e566-4020-9937-365c91a8f123> <https://schema.org/name> "Korea National Environmental Microorganisms Bank" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/906faeb6-e566-4020-9937-365c91a8f123> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "KEMB" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/906faeb6-e566-4020-9937-365c91a8f123> <https://schema.org/description> "KEMB is established microbial and genetic resource center for environmental industries. Recently the demand of the microorganism is increasing according to the activation of environmental-industry. Collection and conservation of native environmental microorganisms (from water, soil, marine) and genetic resources. Construction of systematic management system for effective conservation and application of microbiological resources for environmental industries Promotion of research and industrial activity by utilizing environmental microbial and genetic resources Accomplishment of ecological recovery through constructing ecofriendly bioremediation system substituting chemical treatments by supplying basic microbial resources. There are 10,336 strains in the bank, including photosynthetic bacteria, xenobiotics degrading bacteria, nutrition salts degrading marine bacteria, odor degrading bacteria, and isolated bacteria from environments, materials, animals and humans. All specimens are kept in a single collection with a single numbering system and require no collection codes." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9415f4c0-91e4-4d58-afb2-b263bb96075b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9415f4c0-91e4-4d58-afb2-b263bb96075b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9415f4c0-91e4-4d58-afb2-b263bb96075b> <https://schema.org/name> "Korea Animal Bioresource Bank" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9415f4c0-91e4-4d58-afb2-b263bb96075b> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "ABRB" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9415f4c0-91e4-4d58-afb2-b263bb96075b> <https://schema.org/description> "Animal Bio Resources Bank(ABRB), one of the Korean National Research Resources Bank ,which was established in 2007 and started to work in 2007. The objectives of this ABRB are 1) to develop animal bio-resources and house it. 2) International cooperation study for evaluation on bio-resources 3) Secure and provide of bio - resources in domestic and foreign country 4) Construct of net work in animal bio-resources for livestock industry 5) Promote for national health." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9b1eb1f7-80ad-4463-be71-483e40bf521a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9b1eb1f7-80ad-4463-be71-483e40bf521a> <https://schema.org/name> "California Academy of Sciences" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9b1eb1f7-80ad-4463-be71-483e40bf521a> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "DS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9b1eb1f7-80ad-4463-be71-483e40bf521a> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated June 2008. In 1976 Dudley Herbarium (DS) transferred to CAS on loan. DS and CAS fully integrated and operated as a unit, even though ownership remains with respective institutions. Dudley Herbarium specimens should be cited as DS. Dudley Herbarium contains about 750 000 specimens; this number is included in the total given for CAS. All correspondence relative to loans and exchanges should be with CAS. CI incorporated in DS. Specimens from CI, including vouchers of J. C. Clausen, D. D. Keck, W. M. Hiesey, and M. A. Nobs, should be cited as DS. DS algae transferred to UC. DS fungi transferred to BPI. DS arctic bryophytes (4580 specimens) transferred to NY in 1968. W. R. Dudley's New York state bryophytes transferred to NYS. Remainder of DS bryophytes transferred to UBC and CAS. Library owns private collection of Adolf Engler's reprints. Contact Debra Trock, dtrock@calacademy.org" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9b1eb1f7-80ad-4463-be71-483e40bf521a> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-122.466789 37.770241)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9b88f228-7780-4eac-ad18-86ab5c9354dd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9b88f228-7780-4eac-ad18-86ab5c9354dd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9b88f228-7780-4eac-ad18-86ab5c9354dd> <https://schema.org/name> "King Faisal University" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9b88f228-7780-4eac-ad18-86ab5c9354dd> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "KFU" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9b88f228-7780-4eac-ad18-86ab5c9354dd> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/00dn43547> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9b88f228-7780-4eac-ad18-86ab5c9354dd> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3070702> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9cfe8cbf-35ff-4d93-b932-cb05d91b7922> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9cfe8cbf-35ff-4d93-b932-cb05d91b7922> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9cfe8cbf-35ff-4d93-b932-cb05d91b7922> <https://schema.org/name> "Australian Museum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9cfe8cbf-35ff-4d93-b932-cb05d91b7922> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "AM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9cfe8cbf-35ff-4d93-b932-cb05d91b7922> <https://schema.org/description> "The Australian Museum is a dynamic source of reliable scientific information and a touchstone for informed debate about some of the most pressing environmental and social challenges facing our region: the loss of biodiversity, a changing climate and the search for cultural identity. Underpinning our research is an irreplaceable collection of international standing: over 22 million objects representing a timeline of the environmental and cultural histories of the Australian and Pacific regions. Our collection holds many objects from Indigenous Australia and the Pacific, a record of human diversity and a living wellspring for regional cultural diversity. It contains irreplaceable fossils, minerals, meteorites and gemstones that provide a geological perspective of the planet. It houses representative specimens of native Australian mammals, birds, reptiles, fish and countless invertebrates that tell many stories about our unique wildlife." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9cfe8cbf-35ff-4d93-b932-cb05d91b7922> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(151.213113 -33.874131)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9d1ff333-51bf-4cf3-836e-fe38dd2e6bc0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9d1ff333-51bf-4cf3-836e-fe38dd2e6bc0> <https://schema.org/name> "Australian National Algae Culture Collection" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9d1ff333-51bf-4cf3-836e-fe38dd2e6bc0> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "ANACC" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9d1ff333-51bf-4cf3-836e-fe38dd2e6bc0> <https://schema.org/description> "Formerly Known as CSIRO Collection of Living Micro-algae (acronym CS). For historical continuity \"CS-\" is maintained as the strain code prefix. ANACC uses a single numbering system that does not require collection codes. Representatives of most marine microalgae classes and several freshwater classes including noxious cyanobacteria" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9d1ff333-51bf-4cf3-836e-fe38dd2e6bc0> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/01qv3ez98> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9d1ff333-51bf-4cf3-836e-fe38dd2e6bc0> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q64085930> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9ed8b7bc-0ac6-41d6-b2b5-f9f9f9db7d00> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9ed8b7bc-0ac6-41d6-b2b5-f9f9f9db7d00> <https://schema.org/name> "Fungal Genetics Stock Center" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9ed8b7bc-0ac6-41d6-b2b5-f9f9f9db7d00> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "FGSC" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9ed8b7bc-0ac6-41d6-b2b5-f9f9f9db7d00> <https://schema.org/description> "The FGSC holds over 70,000 isolates of filamentous fungi including classical mutant, wild type, and gene deletion mutants for several fungi. Being a genetics repository, it emphasizes diversity of genetics and not diversity of organisms. Holdings include 48,000 Magnaporthe isolates, 20,000 Neurospora isolates, and several thousand Cryptococcus, Candida and Aspergillus strains." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9fbe6df1-a60d-4d9a-942e-a0d086edfe90> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9fbe6df1-a60d-4d9a-942e-a0d086edfe90> <https://schema.org/name> "Landcare Research" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9fbe6df1-a60d-4d9a-942e-a0d086edfe90> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "LCR" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9fbe6df1-a60d-4d9a-942e-a0d086edfe90> <https://schema.org/description> "Landcare Research was originally part of the Department of Scientific and Industrial Research (DSIR), but was established as an independent organisation when the Crown Research Institutes were created in 1992. As part of that process, it was semi-commercialised, and now operates as a government-owned company rather than as a government department. The commercialisation has led to greater emphasis on financial viability, and Landcare Research is employed by various private groups to provide advice and information." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a24accd6-a4f5-4afe-a9bb-e6a19a27aa6e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a24accd6-a4f5-4afe-a9bb-e6a19a27aa6e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a24accd6-a4f5-4afe-a9bb-e6a19a27aa6e> <https://schema.org/name> "Korea Cosmeceutical Material Bank" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a24accd6-a4f5-4afe-a9bb-e6a19a27aa6e> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "KCMB" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a24accd6-a4f5-4afe-a9bb-e6a19a27aa6e> <https://schema.org/description> "Korea Cosmeceutical Material Bank recruits professional researchers, constructs system for preservation and finances, and promotes supply systems for herbal medicine resources, and collects several herbal cosmeceutical materials, controls herbal medicine resource, and joins works of other researchers. Korea Cosmeceutical Material Bank develops herbal cosmeceutical materials, promotes academic and industrial activities by supplying basic materials for research and industrial applications, and utilizes the on-line system on the basis of web database. And also we supplies services of herbal medicine resource for researchers, establishes the database system for the cosmetic materials, and provides information." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a886617f-d4a9-4f12-94e6-97e8a5180170> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a886617f-d4a9-4f12-94e6-97e8a5180170> <https://schema.org/name> "c/o North Queensland Naturalists' Club" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a886617f-d4a9-4f12-94e6-97e8a5180170> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "CAIRNS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a886617f-d4a9-4f12-94e6-97e8a5180170> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated Apr 2008. CAIRNS transferred to QRS in 1971, and further transferred to CNS in 2007. Contact Frank A. Zich, frank.zich@csiro.au" .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ab8b25c4-f95e-437b-82df-5aed3c9031ec> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ab8b25c4-f95e-437b-82df-5aed3c9031ec> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ab8b25c4-f95e-437b-82df-5aed3c9031ec> <https://schema.org/name> "Florida Museum of Natural History- Zoology, Paleontology & Paleobotany" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ab8b25c4-f95e-437b-82df-5aed3c9031ec> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "UF" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ab8b25c4-f95e-437b-82df-5aed3c9031ec> <https://schema.org/description> "(formerly Florida State Museum) The Florida Museum of Natural History is part of the University of Florida and uses three institutional codes: FLAS (Herbarium); FLMNH (Anthropology, including zooarchaeology; and UF (modern invertebrates, modern vertebrates, fossil invertebrates, fossil vertebrates, fossil plants). There are multiple collections in UF that require collection codes." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b279b36b-11d9-4c4d-94c2-2a8ec71ca4c3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b279b36b-11d9-4c4d-94c2-2a8ec71ca4c3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b279b36b-11d9-4c4d-94c2-2a8ec71ca4c3> <https://schema.org/name> "Ginseng Resource Bank" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b279b36b-11d9-4c4d-94c2-2a8ec71ca4c3> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "GRB" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b279b36b-11d9-4c4d-94c2-2a8ec71ca4c3> <https://schema.org/description> "Previously used acronyms: GB, GGRB. Ginseng Resource Bank (GRB) is a scientific bank for collection and distribution of various resources related to ginseng, which includes ginseng seeds, transformed ginseng, varieties, regenerated plants, whole ginseng plants grown in field in Panax genus. GRB is preparing and providing genomic DNA, cDNA, EST and BAC library of ginseng. GRB is also providing related materials including ginsenoside saponin, ginseng publication list and literatures. GRB is hoping to construct database for ginseng research and to operate in the hub of ginseng world." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b55f8683-b79b-4b70-a9f5-be1d5a4dcf3f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b55f8683-b79b-4b70-a9f5-be1d5a4dcf3f> <https://schema.org/name> "Korea Marine Microalgae Culture Center" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b55f8683-b79b-4b70-a9f5-be1d5a4dcf3f> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "KMMCC" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b55f8683-b79b-4b70-a9f5-be1d5a4dcf3f> <https://schema.org/description> "Speciality is live food culture in mariculture. Main activity of KMMCC is collection marine microalgae, but we have also collected fresh and estuary microalgae and zooplankton , which are useful as a live food organism for aquaculture." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b6d73ad2-2b45-45b0-9a72-6bc7f6251038> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b6d73ad2-2b45-45b0-9a72-6bc7f6251038> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b6d73ad2-2b45-45b0-9a72-6bc7f6251038> <https://schema.org/name> "Oberösterreichische Landes-Kultur GmbH" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b6d73ad2-2b45-45b0-9a72-6bc7f6251038> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "LMOB" .
