<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ca3714ed-d1af-485e-97ff-5f19be667b29> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q655542> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cd1bb9e8-49b5-4266-8871-a44a992153d5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cd1bb9e8-49b5-4266-8871-a44a992153d5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cd1bb9e8-49b5-4266-8871-a44a992153d5> <https://schema.org/name> "Australian National Fish Collection" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cd1bb9e8-49b5-4266-8871-a44a992153d5> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "CSIRO" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cd1bb9e8-49b5-4266-8871-a44a992153d5> <https://schema.org/description> "The Australian National Fish Collection (formerly the I.S.R. Munro Ichthyological Collection) contains more than 161,000 fish specimens representing more than 3,500 species. It was established by Dr I.S.R. Munro in the 1940's, when the CSIRO Division of Fisheries was based in Cronulla (Sydney, NSW). It is now housed at the CSIRO Marine Laboratories in Hobart (Tasmania). Most specimens were collected during CSIRO surveys and on research vessels, notably Fairwind (Papua New Guinea region, 1948-1950), Stanley Fowler (tropical Australia, 1948-1950), Rama (Gulf of Carpentaria, 1963-1965), FRV Courageous (1975-1979), FRV Soela (1979-1989), FRV Southern Surveyor (1990 to 2013) and RV Investigator (2015 to present). Some specimens were acquired from fisheries observers, fishers and via donations. The collection’s strengths are deep-water fishes and sharks and rays. The largest part of the collection is from Australian waters. There are also collections from Papua New Guinea, the Bismarck Archipelago, Solomon Islands, New Zealand, Antarctic waters and south-east Asia (particularly Indonesia, Malaysia and Taiwan). In addition to adult fishes, the collection contains fish larvae and an extensive collection of photographs and x-rays." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cd1bb9e8-49b5-4266-8871-a44a992153d5> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/05hdbs804> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cd1bb9e8-49b5-4266-8871-a44a992153d5> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q106411842> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ceac6f9f-a4d0-453c-a232-c864bd10feaa> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ceac6f9f-a4d0-453c-a232-c864bd10feaa> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ceac6f9f-a4d0-453c-a232-c864bd10feaa> <https://schema.org/name> "Instituto de Biología, Universidad Nacional Autónoma de México" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ceac6f9f-a4d0-453c-a232-c864bd10feaa> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "IBUNAM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ceac6f9f-a4d0-453c-a232-c864bd10feaa> <https://schema.org/description> "The Universidad Nacional Autónoma de México (UNAM) is a public institution whose substantive tasks are teaching, research, and the dissemination of culture. It is currently the largest and most important university in Mexico and Latin America and is recognized in the academic world as a university of excellence. UNAM has 27 museums open to the public, as well as galleries and collections of many types, and preserves museum spaces such as botanical gardens, planetariums, observatories and other facilities for the promotion of science and culture. One of UNAM's strengths is the National Biodiversity Pavilion, which houses four national biological collections (fish, amphibians and reptiles, birds and mammals) consisting of about 130,000 specimens in total, documenting Mexican biodiversity and other parts of the world. The National Collections make available to the qualified scientific community museum specimens from Mexico and adjacent regions, in optimal state of conservation and with the appropriate standard of care, including databases available on the Internet with information associated with the specimens. Mainly Mexico, and New World and many regions in the Old World. Numerous taxa of plants, animals, fungi, fossils and microorganisms" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ceac6f9f-a4d0-453c-a232-c864bd10feaa> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/01tmp8f25> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ceac6f9f-a4d0-453c-a232-c864bd10feaa> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q21065594> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ceac6f9f-a4d0-453c-a232-c864bd10feaa> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-99.194399 19.32071)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ceac6f9f-a4d0-453c-a232-c864bd10feaa> <https://schema.org/logo> <https://members.oeglobal.org/media/logos/UNAM_LJuCFmv.png> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d044be1d-484b-4ecf-89b9-5b63054de960> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d044be1d-484b-4ecf-89b9-5b63054de960> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d044be1d-484b-4ecf-89b9-5b63054de960> <https://schema.org/name> "Frost Entomological Museum, Penn State University" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d044be1d-484b-4ecf-89b9-5b63054de960> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "PSUC" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d044be1d-484b-4ecf-89b9-5b63054de960> <https://schema.org/description> "The research collection comprises over 1,300,000 specimens of insects representing at least 20,000 species. Specimens are pinned, slide mounted, and liquid preserved in alcohol with dried artifacts. Some important collection holdings include the George and Alice Beatty Odonata Collection, John Pepper Aphid Collection, George F. Patterson butterfly collection, K.C. Kim Anoplura Collection, archival collections from major inventory and assessment projects including several national parks and a PA National Guard Training Center and others." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d044be1d-484b-4ecf-89b9-5b63054de960> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-77.8624 40.8031)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d207ceed-42b6-4765-84e0-2b5e958a5c3e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d207ceed-42b6-4765-84e0-2b5e958a5c3e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d207ceed-42b6-4765-84e0-2b5e958a5c3e> <https://schema.org/name> "Michigan State University Museum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d207ceed-42b6-4765-84e0-2b5e958a5c3e> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "MSU" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d207ceed-42b6-4765-84e0-2b5e958a5c3e> <https://schema.org/description> "Mammalogy, Ornithology, and Vertebrate Paleontology collections. Separate Institutional acronym for Ichthyology and Herpetology (see MSUM- http://grbio.org/institution/michigan-state-university-museum-0). Worldwide, especially vascular plants of North America, Bahama Islands, Mexico, Guatemala, and Borneo; lichens and some bryophytes of North America, Patagonia and Straits of Magellan, island groups of sub-Antarctic, West Indies, Juan Fernandez Islands, Canary Islands, and Australasia. Vertebrate Paleontology, ornithology, mammology, ichthyology and herpetology collections." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d207ceed-42b6-4765-84e0-2b5e958a5c3e> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q75623502> .
