<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d6fee9d0-9f77-475e-b1d2-3dd7d90afc2b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d6fee9d0-9f77-475e-b1d2-3dd7d90afc2b> <https://schema.org/name> "Montana State Entomology Collection" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d6fee9d0-9f77-475e-b1d2-3dd7d90afc2b> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "MTEC" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d6fee9d0-9f77-475e-b1d2-3dd7d90afc2b> <https://schema.org/description> "The Montana Entomology Collection is the insect, arthropod and invertebrate collection for Montana State University" .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d85d14b8-a5ed-48de-bc99-351fd00c71d7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d85d14b8-a5ed-48de-bc99-351fd00c71d7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d85d14b8-a5ed-48de-bc99-351fd00c71d7> <https://schema.org/name> "Ohio Wesleyan University Museum of Natural History" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d85d14b8-a5ed-48de-bc99-351fd00c71d7> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "OWU" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d85d14b8-a5ed-48de-bc99-351fd00c71d7> <https://schema.org/description> "The Ohio Wesleyan University Museum of Natural History dates to 1847 and includes specimens of all major animal taxa, though it is strongly focused on birds of Central Ohio. The museum collections are actively used for teaching, exhibition, and research. Largely focused on Central Ohio, with historic specimens from Australia, Palestine, Hawaii, and elsewhere. The zoological collections are primarily focused on birds, but with representative collections of mammals, reptiles, amphibians, fish, and invertebrates. The fossil collections largely represent local fossil fish and invertebrates." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d85d14b8-a5ed-48de-bc99-351fd00c71d7> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-83.105232 40.2677)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/db6a0ab1-a04a-487e-ad12-65dd5bff0e3f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/db6a0ab1-a04a-487e-ad12-65dd5bff0e3f> <https://schema.org/name> "ILSbio, LLC Biobank" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/db6a0ab1-a04a-487e-ad12-65dd5bff0e3f> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "ILSbio" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/db6a0ab1-a04a-487e-ad12-65dd5bff0e3f> <https://schema.org/description> "ILSbio, LLC is a 15 year old biotech company dedicated to providing high quality, well documented biospecimens and support services necessary for advancing translational research. The purpose of ILSbio is to continually push scientific discovery from the lab into clinical practice by facilitating innovation in diagnostics, prognostics and therapeutics." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/dd650e9f-2fb6-41c9-9dba-100c23a1393a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
