<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/1f322b47-5ece-4e82-927e-32114d08ebd6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/1f322b47-5ece-4e82-927e-32114d08ebd6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/1f322b47-5ece-4e82-927e-32114d08ebd6> <https://schema.org/name> "Kuopio Natural History Museum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/1f322b47-5ece-4e82-927e-32114d08ebd6> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "KUO" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/1f322b47-5ece-4e82-927e-32114d08ebd6> <https://schema.org/description> "The Kuopio Museum of Natural History helps to understand the diversity of life. Extensive collections are the core of museum work and the foundation of natural history. Collections reflect environmental change over time. Their study provides information on natural phenomena and the interaction between humans and nature. Since 2020, the Kuopio Natural History Museum has been responsible for the regions of North Savo, North Karelia, South Savo and South Karelia. Its mission is to promote regional museum activities and to provide expert services to local museums, government and the general public. The results of regional work are used in the implementation of natural science exhibitions, as well as in collection and expert services related to natural heritage and biodiversity information." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/1f322b47-5ece-4e82-927e-32114d08ebd6> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q58636577> .
