<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b6cb4c2a-5927-470b-834c-aed6d5638765> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b6cb4c2a-5927-470b-834c-aed6d5638765> <https://schema.org/name> "Centro de Investigación para la Salud en América Latina CISeAL de la Pontificia Universidad Católica del Ecuador" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b6cb4c2a-5927-470b-834c-aed6d5638765> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "CISEAL" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b6cb4c2a-5927-470b-834c-aed6d5638765> <https://schema.org/description> "The Center for Health Research in Latin America (CISeAL) is an international platform dedicated to fostering scientific collaborations that advance knowledge and improve public health. In Ecuador, a country of immense biodiversity with around 17,000 plant species, many of which have applications in traditional medicine, CISeAL focuses on researching bioactive compounds with therapeutic potential. These compounds, both from plant and animal sources, possess antimicrobial, anti-inflammatory, anticancer, and other properties, with low toxicity. In particular, alkaloids and peptides from animals like frogs and certain endophytic microorganisms show great promise for treating diseases and improving public health. Additionally, viruses have potential in biotechnology and environmental conservation. CISeAL conducts research focused on infectious and chronic diseases, as well as the development of infrastructure and personnel training. Its work complies with international bioethical and biosafety standards. Ecuador, with its rich biodiversity, offers great potential for discovering new bioactive compounds, which are crucial for developing new treatments and sustainable solutions in medicine and agriculture. CISeAL's infrastructure and scientific collaborations are key to this progress, benefiting both the scientific community and society in general." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b6cb4c2a-5927-470b-834c-aed6d5638765> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-78.489532 -0.20849)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

