<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bf35502f-004a-4fa3-a239-b270ec85f2bc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bf35502f-004a-4fa3-a239-b270ec85f2bc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bf35502f-004a-4fa3-a239-b270ec85f2bc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bf35502f-004a-4fa3-a239-b270ec85f2bc> <https://schema.org/name> "Marine Biology Station of Inhaca" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bf35502f-004a-4fa3-a239-b270ec85f2bc> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "EBMI" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bf35502f-004a-4fa3-a239-b270ec85f2bc> <https://schema.org/description> "The Estação de Biologia Marítima de Inhaca (EBMI) is a marine research station on Inhaca Island, Mozambique, managed by the Universidade Eduardo Mondlane (UEM). Established in 1951, EBMI is among the oldest marine research facilities on the African continent and holds historical significance as Mozambique’s first institution dedicated to marine biology and conservation research. Located near Maputo, the station is equipped to support in-depth fieldwork and laboratory studies of the region's diverse marine ecosystems, such as coral reefs, mangroves, and seagrass beds. As part of UEM's Faculty of Sciences, EBMI facilitates academic and research activities for both national and international scientists and students. Its modest facilities include laboratories, a library, and accommodation, making it a practical base for researchers working in the field. EBMI also hosts a small museum with a valuable collection of marine biodiversity specimens, some dating back decades. This collection documents the ecological history of Mozambique’s coastal waters and serves as an educational resource, showcasing the region's natural heritage and the longstanding research efforts to preserve it. EBMI's work extends beyond academic research; it collaborates with local communities, conservation groups, and global institutions to promote sustainable marine practices. Its role is essential in preserving Mozambique's coastal ecosystems and fostering awareness about the importance of marine conservation in the Western Indian Ocean." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bf35502f-004a-4fa3-a239-b270ec85f2bc> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(32.902057 -26.045168)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

