<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/0b5e21e6-295e-4a20-b455-cc6155d9a2b2> <https://schema.org/name> "\"Ioulia & Alexandros N. Diomidis\" Botanical Garden" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/0b5e21e6-295e-4a20-b455-cc6155d9a2b2> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "NKUA-BGIAD" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/0b5e21e6-295e-4a20-b455-cc6155d9a2b2> <https://schema.org/description> "The botanical gardern is located in Haidari, on the Northern slopes of Mount Aigaleo and at a distance of 8 km from Athens. It is the largest Botanical Garden of Greece and of the entire Eastern Mediterranean, which operates today, occupying an area of ​​1,860 acres. The Garden is a member of the International Union of Botanic Gardens - BGCI. Approximately 11% (about 20 hectares) of the total Garden area has been used to form the typical botanic garden hosting more than 2500 plant taxa. This part of the Garden is separated into the following sections: Arboretum Ornamental Plants Section Historic Plants Section Medicinal & Aromatic Plants Plants and economy Taxonomy Section Greenhouse Nursery " .
