<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9bb40d56-3dcb-410f-b0fc-5e6b3d10b65e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9bb40d56-3dcb-410f-b0fc-5e6b3d10b65e> <https://schema.org/name> "Istituto per la Protezione sostenibile delle piante di Bari" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9bb40d56-3dcb-410f-b0fc-5e6b3d10b65e> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "CNR-IPSP-BA" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9bb40d56-3dcb-410f-b0fc-5e6b3d10b65e> <https://schema.org/description> "The Institute for Sustainable Protection of Plants (CNR-IPSP) is aimed at valorising plants of agricultural and forestry interest, strengthening natural antagonisms and biocontrol methods of plant parasites and weeds, improving the quality and quantity of agri-food production, selecting and remediating valuable plant germplasm, characterizing and producing bio-molecules of agro-industrial interest, mitigating the impacts of global change, promoting sustainable and environmentally friendly growth. Activities at CNR-IPSP are focused to integrate specific knowledge in the sectors of nematology, entomology, pathology, viral and virus-like phytopathogens, mycorrhizal fungi and bacteria, biostimulators and biofertilizers and defense from environmental stress." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9bb40d56-3dcb-410f-b0fc-5e6b3d10b65e> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(16.888615 41.10226)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
