<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c29e0c07-f7e3-4f57-b2a5-79212756ce98> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c29e0c07-f7e3-4f57-b2a5-79212756ce98> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c29e0c07-f7e3-4f57-b2a5-79212756ce98> <https://schema.org/name> "Duke Lemur Center Museum of Natural History" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c29e0c07-f7e3-4f57-b2a5-79212756ce98> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "DPC" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c29e0c07-f7e3-4f57-b2a5-79212756ce98> <https://schema.org/description> "The DLC Museum of Natural History (DLCMNH) is a research collection used to understand our evolutionary journey as primates. Primates are the group of mammals that includes lemurs, monkeys, apes, and humans. For more than forty years, museum scientists have conducted fieldwork around the world, targeting major branches in the primate family tree for deeper exploration. Our collection includes 55 million year-old, lemur-like primate fossils from Wyoming; 37 to 28 million year-old anthropoid fossils from Egypt; 19 to 7 million year-old ape fossils from Egypt and India; 13 million year-old New World monkeys from Colombia; and 10,000 to 500 year-old lemur fossils from Madagascar" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c29e0c07-f7e3-4f57-b2a5-79212756ce98> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-78.919631 36.014574)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/147eb5bf-dbc5-4a56-b49e-73fe4e4b8f29> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/147eb5bf-dbc5-4a56-b49e-73fe4e4b8f29> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/147eb5bf-dbc5-4a56-b49e-73fe4e4b8f29> <https://schema.org/name> "Moldova State University, Faculty of Biology and Geoscience" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/147eb5bf-dbc5-4a56-b49e-73fe4e4b8f29> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "USMB" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/147eb5bf-dbc5-4a56-b49e-73fe4e4b8f29> <https://schema.org/description> "The faculty was founded in 1946, simultaneously with the State University of Moldova. Its formation is linked to the names of famous scientists - academician N. Dimo ​​and professors V. Andreev, I. Vul. Over the years, the faculty has trained over 6,000 young specialists, including from many countries abroad. One of the priorities of the Faculty of Biology and Pedology is the involvement of students in the research activity. Within the study programs, mandatory and optional theoretical courses are offered that allow students to be trained in the scientific research carried out in the \"Life Sciences\" Research Center. A real treasure of the faculty is the Museum of Natural Sciences, which includes the sections of Geology, Soil Sciences, Botany and Zoology, with an impressive number of exhibits from around the world. Graduates have the opportunity to work in different fields of the national economy, in the subdivisions of the Ministry of Agriculture, Regional Development and the Environment, in the research institutions of AŞM, in production units in the field of natural sciences, etc., but also as biology teachers or geography in pre-university and university education institutions." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/147eb5bf-dbc5-4a56-b49e-73fe4e4b8f29> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(28.824913 47.019614)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5a0933da-68ba-44d5-89da-59f76a3f374a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5a0933da-68ba-44d5-89da-59f76a3f374a> <https://schema.org/name> "Kalsnava Arboretum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5a0933da-68ba-44d5-89da-59f76a3f374a> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "LVKA" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5a0933da-68ba-44d5-89da-59f76a3f374a> <https://schema.org/description> "Kalsnava Arboretum is a unique dendrological collection created with the main goal - to preserve and enrich the collection of local and foreign tree plants. The establishment of Kalsnava arboretum plantations was started already in 1975 and the current area of Kalsnava arboretum is 148.66 ha. According to the data of the dendrological inventory conducted in 2020, a total of more than 22,000 specimens and groups belonging to more than 2,800 tree and hardy perennial taxa from more than 200 genera have been registered in the territory of Kalsnava Arboretum. A large part of the taxa planted in the Kalsnava arboretum are considered to be the most outstanding specimens of the respective taxon in Latvia due to their wild origin, rarity, excellent acclimatization ability or other reasons. The dendrological collection is regularly supplemented with new plant material." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5a0933da-68ba-44d5-89da-59f76a3f374a> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q29075522> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5a0933da-68ba-44d5-89da-59f76a3f374a> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(25.959278 56.686806)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a7a495a2-fec4-4380-aee3-968766a6306c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a7a495a2-fec4-4380-aee3-968766a6306c> <https://schema.org/name> "Institute of Microbiology of the Ministry of Science and Education of the Republic of Azerbaijan" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a7a495a2-fec4-4380-aee3-968766a6306c> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "AZMBI" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a7a495a2-fec4-4380-aee3-968766a6306c> <https://schema.org/description> "The foundation of ANAS was laid in 1972. It is typical that many fields of general microbiology in Azerbaijan were developed in small units in the Institute of Soil Science and Agrochemistry, Zoology of ANAS for up to 20 years, but in February 1972 by the decision of the Presidium of ANAS the Department of Microbiology was established and operated under the same name until 1994. Famous academician M.G.Ganiyev and doctor of biological sciences, professor Nisakhanim Mehdiyeva played a great role in the establishment of the department. On November 2, 1994, the Department of Microbiology was granted the status of Institute by the Resolution of the Cabinet of Ministers of the Republic of Azerbaijan № 375 and on December 12, 1995 it was registered by the Ministry of Justice of the Republic of Azerbaijan as a state institution (Certificate № D-889 was obtained). At present, the Institute of Microbiology continues its activity as a structural unit of ANAS within the Department of Biological and Medical Sciences of ANAS. To conduct fundamental and practical research in the field of microbiology and biotechnology." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a7a495a2-fec4-4380-aee3-968766a6306c> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(49.8196 40.3655)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/05eb7948-eb6f-4d90-95a6-a6f062a89640> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/05eb7948-eb6f-4d90-95a6-a6f062a89640> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/05eb7948-eb6f-4d90-95a6-a6f062a89640> <https://schema.org/name> "Museum of Natural History named after Hasanbey Zardabi" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/05eb7948-eb6f-4d90-95a6-a6f062a89640> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "MNHAZ" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/05eb7948-eb6f-4d90-95a6-a6f062a89640> <https://schema.org/description> "Initially, the Museum functioned as a local history educational club in 1920. The natural history museum itself was founded in 1930. The museum has two departments: a geology department that has samples of metallic and nonmetallic natural resources and minerals and rocks of Azerbaijan and a zoology department. The general collection of the museum numbers more than 1400 different items. The biological department exhibits numerous skeletons and fragments of animal bones found during field work and treated by researchers. The oldest exhibit is the teeth of an ichthyosaur from the Cretaceous period, more than 120 million years old." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/05eb7948-eb6f-4d90-95a6-a6f062a89640> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(49.829 40.35962)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3333138b-63c4-4ef5-812f-340c5ab81595> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3333138b-63c4-4ef5-812f-340c5ab81595> <https://schema.org/name> "Regione Sardegna" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3333138b-63c4-4ef5-812f-340c5ab81595> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "SAR" .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b57d182a-5ff1-4426-8da1-35a0dae1df69> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b57d182a-5ff1-4426-8da1-35a0dae1df69> <https://schema.org/name> "Istituto per la Protezione sostenibile delle piante di Sesto Fiorentino" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b57d182a-5ff1-4426-8da1-35a0dae1df69> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "CNR-IPSP-FI" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b57d182a-5ff1-4426-8da1-35a0dae1df69> <https://schema.org/description> "IPSP studies plant response to biotic and abiotic stress factors, with the aim of identifying mechanisms of resistance and adaptation, to promote of plant health in agriculture and forestry. This implies strengthening the use of natural enemies and beneficial microorganisms in integrated pest management, selecting and recovering valuable plant germplasm, identifying bio-molecules of agricultural or industrial interest, and ultimately promoting a sustainable and environmentally friendly growth." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b57d182a-5ff1-4426-8da1-35a0dae1df69> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/008fjbg42> .
