<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/29b3cd27-2385-45a0-8466-5275a75d0f19> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "UNIBO-BOT" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/29b3cd27-2385-45a0-8466-5275a75d0f19> <https://schema.org/description> "The Botanical Garden and Herbarium of the University of Bologna, established in the 16th century, are among the oldest in Europe. The Botanical Garden covers an area of two hectares reaching as far as the ancient city walls. The gardens house thematic collections, reconstructions of natural habitats and greenhouses with tropical, succulent and carnivorous plants. The Herbarium, comprising more than 100,000 dried plant specimens, also houses the valuable collections of Ulisse Aldrovandi (1522-1605) and Antonio Bertoloni (1775-1868)" .
