<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/062f9cd2-ba0e-48ef-8028-dddbbf2140c5> <https://schema.org/name> "Stazione Zoologica Anton Dohrn" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/062f9cd2-ba0e-48ef-8028-dddbbf2140c5> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "SZN" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/062f9cd2-ba0e-48ef-8028-dddbbf2140c5> <https://schema.org/description> "The Anton Dohrn Zoological Station in Naples, established in 1872 by German scientist Anton Dohrn, is a public research organization overseen by the Italian Ministry of Education, Universities, and Research. Recognized as a leading institution in marine biology and ecology, it was founded to promote basic research by hosting scientists studying marine organisms. Today, its mission is to conduct fundamental research on marine biodiversity, biological evolution, and ecosystem dynamics using an integrated and interdisciplinary approach. The station also facilitates access to marine organisms for the global scientific community and offers advanced training in its areas of expertise." .
