<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3eae3cc9-204b-404e-afba-bbc168ae3c24> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3eae3cc9-204b-404e-afba-bbc168ae3c24> <https://schema.org/name> "Biotechnology Institute, National Academy of Sciences of the Kyrgyz Republic" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3eae3cc9-204b-404e-afba-bbc168ae3c24> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "BINASK" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3eae3cc9-204b-404e-afba-bbc168ae3c24> <https://schema.org/description> "The main task of the Institute of Biotechnology of the National Academy of Sciences of the Republic of Kazakhstan is to conduct fundamental and applied research on the development of new means and methods for protecting the health of animals and their habitats from dangerous and especially dangerous pathogens using biotechnology methods. This includes the development of import-substituting technologies, biologically active substances, conservation of biodiversity and genetic resources of animals, plants, and microorganisms, improving ecological, biological, and food safety, creating new breeds of agricultural animals, increasing their reproductive capacity, and disease prevention. Currently, at the Institute of Biotechnology, there are six laboratories: Biotechnology and Nutrition, Genetics and Biotechnology, Biochemistry, Microbiology, Plant Biotechnology, and Virology. The main directions of scientific activity include: Monitoring of natural foci and specially protected areas, and identification of valuable living organisms for the genetic resources bank. Designing vaccines and other biological means of protection against infectious and particularly dangerous diseases of agricultural animals. Establishing databases and collections of animals within the territory of the Republic. Developing methods for conserving and rational use of plant resources in Kyrgyzstan through the creation of a genetic database. Bio-testing of animals nominated for inclusion in the genetic resources bank of Kyrgyzstan." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3eae3cc9-204b-404e-afba-bbc168ae3c24> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(74.5791 42.8776)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/38fcb96f-1b23-4863-b9b7-22153673d9d5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/38fcb96f-1b23-4863-b9b7-22153673d9d5> <https://schema.org/name> "\"Instituto de Investigación en Zoonosis de la Universidad Central del Ecuador\"" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/38fcb96f-1b23-4863-b9b7-22153673d9d5> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "CIZ-UCE" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/38fcb96f-1b23-4863-b9b7-22153673d9d5> <https://schema.org/description> "The mission of the CIZ-UCE is to develop and strengthen basic and applied research for academic and scientific training in zoonotic diseases, with a focus on one health, one world, in support of Ecuador's public policies. The vision is to lead the processes of diagnosis and prevention of diseases affecting animals, humans and the environment with multi- and transdisciplinary teams. The Institute is located on the third floor of the Day Hospital Building, Ciudadela Universitaria, Universidad Central del Ecuador, Quito, Ecuador. Tissues of wild fauna (birds, mammals, amphibians and reptiles)" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/38fcb96f-1b23-4863-b9b7-22153673d9d5> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-78.505887 -0.199738)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
