<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e1c62e3c-f0af-4c83-8b09-893eeaba5051> <https://schema.org/description> "Thiruvananthapuram Natural History Museum is a scientific institution with an exhaustive collections of current and historical specimens of animals, plants, geology, paleontology, and more. The museum possess an excellent galleries to share the amazing wonders of the natural world with the public. Predominantly from south-western India with a few collections from other parts of India as well as Southeast Asia. Birds, Fishes, Amphibians, Reptiles, and Mammals" .
