<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7db91b7b-05ef-46ac-aec3-6554033f5b7b> <https://schema.org/name> "Institute of Zoology of the Academy of Sciences of the Republic of Uzbekistan" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7db91b7b-05ef-46ac-aec3-6554033f5b7b> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "TASZ" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7db91b7b-05ef-46ac-aec3-6554033f5b7b> <https://schema.org/description> "The main tasks and activities of the Institute of Zoology of the AS RUz: comprehensive study of the fauna of the republic, assessment of the current state and development of scientific and practical recommendations on the sustainable use of wildlife; identification of key zoological areas, development of the scientific basis for the conservation of rare and endemic species of the animal world; development and maintenance of the national information and analytical database of the fauna of the republic, maintenance of the state cadastre for rare and endangered species of wild animals, the Red Book of the Republic of Uzbekistan and monitoring of wildlife; development of innovative technologies to regulate the number of pests, parasites and biodegraders of structures; study of aquatic ecosystems and ecology of aquatic organisms, assessment and monitoring of the gene pool of fish resources of the republic. Fauna of Uzbekistan. all taxons of animal" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7db91b7b-05ef-46ac-aec3-6554033f5b7b> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(69.31 41.344)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bb3cba32-4ee4-49e6-9e1d-5993d715dd07> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bb3cba32-4ee4-49e6-9e1d-5993d715dd07> <https://schema.org/name> "Institute of Botany of the Academy of Sciences of the Republic of Uzbekistan" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bb3cba32-4ee4-49e6-9e1d-5993d715dd07> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "TAS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bb3cba32-4ee4-49e6-9e1d-5993d715dd07> <https://schema.org/description> "The Institute was founded in July 1940. Resolution of the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan № RP-3861 “About measures for further enhancement of activities of Institute of botany of Academy of Sciences of the Republic of Uzbekistan” dated July 17, 2018 was issued in order to enhance the efficiency of plant sciences, to improve the storage conditions of unique plant collections due to international standards, to accelerate the solution of specialized tasks for study, sustainable utilization and conservation of plant biodiversity, as well as to strengthen material-technical base of the Institute of Botany of the Academy of Sciences of the Republic of Uzbekistan. Central Asia, especially Uzbekistan. All taxonomic groups of plant" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bb3cba32-4ee4-49e6-9e1d-5993d715dd07> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/01xgfaw76> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bb3cba32-4ee4-49e6-9e1d-5993d715dd07> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2637170> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/bb3cba32-4ee4-49e6-9e1d-5993d715dd07> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(69.340834 41.336975)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9ce16309-7819-4f90-ae19-7ce23faf3e7c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9ce16309-7819-4f90-ae19-7ce23faf3e7c> <https://schema.org/name> "Caja de Compensación Familiar - Comfenalco Antioquia" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9ce16309-7819-4f90-ae19-7ce23faf3e7c> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "Comfenalco" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9ce16309-7819-4f90-ae19-7ce23faf3e7c> <https://schema.org/description> "La Caja de Compensación Familiar - Comfenalco Antioquia tiene la finalidad de aportar a una transformación social sostenible e incluyente en la que el bienestar sea un bien colectivo que impacte positivamente la vida de los trabajadores, sus familias y la comunidad. Al año 2025, busca ser un aliado para su afiliados en la gestión del bienestar, consolidando un crecimiento sostenible por medio del incremento de la base empresarial, duplicando los ingresos por servicios y creciendo el número de vidas impactadas en los territorios." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a7e364d8-a0ce-44b9-86e3-0ee2b33893e2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a7e364d8-a0ce-44b9-86e3-0ee2b33893e2> <https://schema.org/name> "Federación Nacional de Cacaoteros" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a7e364d8-a0ce-44b9-86e3-0ee2b33893e2> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "Fedecacao" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a7e364d8-a0ce-44b9-86e3-0ee2b33893e2> <https://schema.org/description> "La Federación Nacional de Cacaoteros (Fedecacao) es una Asociación Nacional de carácter gremial, que está integrada por los productores de cacao dentro del territorio colombiano. Tiene la misión de representar y proteger los intereses de los cacaocultores Colombianos, contribuyendo con su desarrollo integral, ofreciendo servicios de extensión rural, investigación y la comercialización del producto a nivel nacional e internacional, contribuyendo con la protección del Medio Ambiente. A su vez, tiene como visión al año 2030 ser una de las organizaciones líderes en el sector agrícola 1) aumentando la presencia en las diferentes zonas del país y el número de agricultores agremiados, preservando el liderazgo, 2) contribuyendo con el desarrollo de una cacaocultura competitiva a través de la innovación, transferencia de tecnología y la renovación de los cultivos, 3) fomentando una mayor sostenibilidad del Gremio en el tiempo, buscando tener presencia en los principales escenarios del sector agrícola y desarrollando mercados promisorios y 4) apostando al crecimiento de la Federación Nacional de Cacaoteros a través del aumento de la comercialización y exportaciones, consecución de proyectos rentables y la apertura de nuevas fronteras en la comercialización del producto." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c9c85429-8f2d-4337-b3e7-54b2e74f2640> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c9c85429-8f2d-4337-b3e7-54b2e74f2640> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c9c85429-8f2d-4337-b3e7-54b2e74f2640> <https://schema.org/name> "Universidad Católica de Manizales" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c9c85429-8f2d-4337-b3e7-54b2e74f2640> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "UCM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c9c85429-8f2d-4337-b3e7-54b2e74f2640> <https://schema.org/description> "La Universidad Católica de Manizales tiene como misión contribuir a la formación integral de la persona desde una visión humanista, científica y cristiana, iluminada por el Evangelio, el Magisterio de la Iglesia y el Carisma Congregacional de las Hermanas de la Caridad Dominicas de la Presentación de la Santísima Virgen. Orienta la academia con criterios de universalidad, humanización del conocimiento, calidad e innovación, para la construcción de nueva ciudadanía como expresión del diálogo entre fe-cultura-vida, para responder a los desafíos de la sociedad contemporánea, en el contexto de un mundo globalizado con sentido social y eclesial. A su vez, su visión es ser, al año 2025, la primera opción de la región, por visibilizar la formación integral desde una perspectiva humanista, científica y cristiana, consolidando una comunidad académica que, desde la personalización liberadora, contribuya a la transformación social, cultural y se constituya como referente nacional e internacional de inclusión y equidad." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cccb8eb0-d9b5-4e10-a83a-4449ee1f4429> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cccb8eb0-d9b5-4e10-a83a-4449ee1f4429> <https://schema.org/name> "Hiwa Museum of Natural History" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cccb8eb0-d9b5-4e10-a83a-4449ee1f4429> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "HIWA" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cccb8eb0-d9b5-4e10-a83a-4449ee1f4429> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q108299880> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/eadfc5e8-da8c-4010-bdd5-a209c1c628f8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/eadfc5e8-da8c-4010-bdd5-a209c1c628f8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/eadfc5e8-da8c-4010-bdd5-a209c1c628f8> <https://schema.org/name> "El-Hawagry M. Personal collection" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/eadfc5e8-da8c-4010-bdd5-a209c1c628f8> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "MSHC" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/eadfc5e8-da8c-4010-bdd5-a209c1c628f8> <https://schema.org/description> "A personal entomology collection of El-Hawagry M. Egypt. Insects" .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/03e794be-bff9-4324-b1c3-40b19b37736a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/03e794be-bff9-4324-b1c3-40b19b37736a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/03e794be-bff9-4324-b1c3-40b19b37736a> <https://schema.org/name> "Faculty of Biology, University of Plovdiv “Paisii Hilendarski”" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/03e794be-bff9-4324-b1c3-40b19b37736a> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "FBUP" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/03e794be-bff9-4324-b1c3-40b19b37736a> <https://schema.org/description> "The Faculty of Biology conducts training and research in various biological areas and currently has seven departments (Human anatomy and physiology, Developmental biology, Biochemistry and Microbiology, Botany and teaching methods in biology, Ecology and environmental conservation, Zoology and Plant physiology and molecular biology). It has several scientific collections held in several departments. At the Department of Biochemistry and Microbiology (MBT), there is the Microbial Culture Collection, at the Department of Botany there is the Plovdiv Algal Culture Collection (PACC), and at the Department of Botany and MBT, there are educational botanical collections of alcohol, formalin and dry preparations of fungi, algae and higher plants, as well as a rich herbarium for training and research work. At the Department of Ecology and Environmental Conservation, there is a Paleontological and Geological collection and two study collections that represent the conservation status of invertebrate and vertebrate animals in Bulgaria. The Department of Zoology possesses and maintains rich scientific and educational collections of vertebrates and invertebrates. The entomological research collections keep rare species and typus material of newly-identified species. Materials from the collection have been deposited in the National Museum of Natural History in Sofia and in other world famous museums (Museum d’histoire naturelle – Geneva, The Natural History Museum – London, Hungarian Natural History Museum – Budapest, Naturhistorisches Museum – Vienna). Rich craniological and skeletal material is stored in the scientific teratology collection. The study collections were established in the very beginning of the founding of the department in 1963 and they have been maintained and constantly enriched by the department staff. Unique specimens from the beginning of the 20th century can be seen, and they were received from the French College in Plovdiv. Prof. B. Gruev, Assoc. Prof. V. Tomov and Assoc. Prof. A. Donev have founded the educational entomological collection, which represents many species of the Bulgarian entomofauna. The ornithological collection, created by Assoc. Prof. A. Darakchiev, contains common Bulgarian bird species." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/03e794be-bff9-4324-b1c3-40b19b37736a> <https://schema.org/logo> <https://bio.uni-plovdiv.bg/wp-content/uploads/2016/03/logoBioEN.png> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d61d1061-2a2e-4fc1-a846-23eebf842b25> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d61d1061-2a2e-4fc1-a846-23eebf842b25> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d61d1061-2a2e-4fc1-a846-23eebf842b25> <https://schema.org/name> "Department of Zoology, University of Karachi" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d61d1061-2a2e-4fc1-a846-23eebf842b25> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "ZM-DOZUOK" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d61d1061-2a2e-4fc1-a846-23eebf842b25> <https://schema.org/description> "the department has a zoological museum which occupies a special place among the Museums of Pakistan Universities. It has a huge collection of vertebrates and invertebrates from James Murray’s collection and substantial collection of fresh water and Marine fauna of Arabian Sea, Persian Gulf and Indian Ocean. During the past 61 years a considerable addition of insects from South-East Area, Pakistan, Bangladesh including Oriental, Trans-Himalayan (Palaearctic) and Ethiopian forms from Lasbella and Mekran Coast, have been added. Work on taxonomy of fishes (freshwater and marine), Insects and nematodes are being undertaken by trained and experienced staff. Collaboration is being maintained with outstanding taxonomists in Japan, Europe, U.S.A. and Canada." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d61d1061-2a2e-4fc1-a846-23eebf842b25> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(67.119521 24.941354)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ede40840-b2ed-4e64-8d7a-1f88197d2f32> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ede40840-b2ed-4e64-8d7a-1f88197d2f32> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ede40840-b2ed-4e64-8d7a-1f88197d2f32> <https://schema.org/name> "Latvian National Museum of Natural History" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ede40840-b2ed-4e64-8d7a-1f88197d2f32> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "LMNH" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ede40840-b2ed-4e64-8d7a-1f88197d2f32> <https://schema.org/description> "The Latvian National Museum of Natural History is one of the oldest multi-disciplinary museums of natural sciences in the Baltics, and it holds the largest collection of natural specimens available to the public in Latvia. The history of the museum dates back to 1845, when representatives of the Baltic German intelligentsia founded the Riga Naturalist Society (Naturforscher-Verein zu Riga) with a museum and library. The museum collects, preserves and stores Latvian and world nature collections, studies the specimens therein, and popularises the museum's collections through exhibitions, and other activities. The museum’s values of discovering, interpreting, and disseminating are the basic tenets of environmental education. The Latvian National Museum of Natural History operates under the auspices of the Ministry of Environmental Protection and Regional Development. The museum’s mission: to conserve and preserve the natural and material cultural values of Latvia that affirm the diversity, history and protection of nature. Through using the resources of the museum, to carry out environmental education by creating awareness in society about the processes that take place in nature, the place and role of humans therein, and to promote the formation of environmental awareness in society." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ede40840-b2ed-4e64-8d7a-1f88197d2f32> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(24.118175 56.949463)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6024a2b0-1540-43ac-b687-c15478f245d3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6024a2b0-1540-43ac-b687-c15478f245d3> <https://schema.org/name> "J.S.S. Arts, Science and Commerce College, Gokak- 591307, Belagavi, Karnataka" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6024a2b0-1540-43ac-b687-c15478f245d3> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "HJSS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6024a2b0-1540-43ac-b687-c15478f245d3> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(74.817504 16.163264)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/475ffe81-ab5b-48fc-b6bc-b27950fcfae1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/475ffe81-ab5b-48fc-b6bc-b27950fcfae1> <https://schema.org/name> "Dobrudja Agricultural Institute, National Centre of Agricultural Science" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/475ffe81-ab5b-48fc-b6bc-b27950fcfae1> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "DAI" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/475ffe81-ab5b-48fc-b6bc-b27950fcfae1> <https://schema.org/description> "Dobrudja Agricultural Institute is a national research center for the selection and agrotechnics of field crops. It is the largest unit in the system of the Bulgarian Agricultural Academy. BASIC ACTIVITIES: the creation of new improved varieties of cereals and legumes, sunflower varieties and hybrids and development of modern technologies for their cultivation; development of new biotechnological methods in the selection of field crops; collection and research of plant genetic resources; production of pre-basic and basic seeds with guaranteed origin and quality; breeding of elite breeds of breeding animals." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/475ffe81-ab5b-48fc-b6bc-b27950fcfae1> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(28.026308 43.653621)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/475ffe81-ab5b-48fc-b6bc-b27950fcfae1> <https://schema.org/logo> <https://dai-gt.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/cropped-Dobrudzhanski_Zemedelski_Institut_General_Tohevo_logo.png> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5d85f0a7-e9c3-4c31-9890-0df14daac108> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5d85f0a7-e9c3-4c31-9890-0df14daac108> <https://schema.org/name> "Institute of Rose and Essential-oil Plants, Ministry of Agriculture" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5d85f0a7-e9c3-4c31-9890-0df14daac108> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "IREOP" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5d85f0a7-e9c3-4c31-9890-0df14daac108> <https://schema.org/description> "The beginning of the future Institute of Roses, Essential and Medical Cultures, Kazanlak was initiated in 1907, from the famous Bulgarian scientist-Konstantin Malkov. At that time, an experimental station of roses was established, which developed into an Institute 60 years later/ 1967/. The main purpose was to develop and assist rose production. At the same time with the first experiments of rose planting, experiments were made with a number of other essential and medical plants. The scientific research works with different officinal plants started later. Today the Institute of Roses, Essential and Medical Cultures is a governmental organization under the direct subordination of the Ministry of Agriculture and Suppliement. It remains one of the main centers for research, applied service and subsidiary activities in the field of Essential Medical plants in Bulgaria. The main activity of the Institute is in the field of research and includes trends as follow: Introduction, selection and reproduction of essential oil and medical plants Creation and support of a gene fund of 216 sorts, presented by 547 samples, 161 essential oil and medical plants varieties. Technology development for essential oil and medical plants. Raw materials processing technology of essential oil and medical plants. Licensed testing laboratory for analyses and certificate issuing for oils, drugs, plant extracts, sowing seeds, cosmetics and pharmaceuticals. Natural cosmetic production. Over than 40 sorts of essential and medical plants are created. The Institute owns the copyright of 19 sorts of them. The Institute of Roses, Essential and Medical Cultures is the main producer for Bulgaria of super qualitative sowing material of essential oil and medical plants, and the only scientific Institute in EU, which is interested in the area of Oil Bearing Rose." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5d85f0a7-e9c3-4c31-9890-0df14daac108> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(25.388519 42.634827)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/632feb8a-ee2f-4771-8193-6c8e2ce9b154> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
