<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9bce3d39-1397-4a96-9850-a0290f59a1b0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9bce3d39-1397-4a96-9850-a0290f59a1b0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9bce3d39-1397-4a96-9850-a0290f59a1b0> <https://schema.org/name> "Haus der Natur" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9bce3d39-1397-4a96-9850-a0290f59a1b0> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "HNS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9bce3d39-1397-4a96-9850-a0290f59a1b0> <https://schema.org/description> "The Haus der Natur museum of natural history has been in existence since 1924. Today the Haus der Natur is a “three-division institution” with a regional and international focus. It encompasses the classical natural history museum, high-quality zoo divisions, and a Science Center with a broad and varied offering. The Haus der Natur plays an important role as a center of specialized knowledge and expertise about the natural world for the city and province of Salzburg. The biodiversity center of Haus der Natur houses the national natural science collections and maintains a comprehensive database containing documentation and analyses of the animal and plant species in the city and province of Salzburg, as well as High Tauern National Park. The collection and biodiversity database focusses on the Austrian province of Salzburg, but also contains data and specimen from all over the world. The following groups of organisms are the main focus of the museum's collections and database: fungi, lichens, vascular plants, mosses, molluscs, odonata, orthoptera, lepidoptera, hymenoptera, coleoptera, amphibians, reptiles, birds and mammals." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9bce3d39-1397-4a96-9850-a0290f59a1b0> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/00hn7pt27> .
