<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/90944dfa-0357-49f9-9c35-0c3183827461> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/90944dfa-0357-49f9-9c35-0c3183827461> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/90944dfa-0357-49f9-9c35-0c3183827461> <https://schema.org/name> "Regional Museum of History - Pleven" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/90944dfa-0357-49f9-9c35-0c3183827461> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "RIM-Pleven" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/90944dfa-0357-49f9-9c35-0c3183827461> <https://schema.org/description> "The appearance of a multitude of smart people from different historical eras is a prerequisite for the development of the museum work in the city of Pleven. In 1903 the Bulgarian Archaeological Society - Pleven branch is founded. The idea is from prof. Ivan Šišmanov, and it was realized by Dr. Paraškev Stoyanov and Jurdan Kantardžiev. The goals of the association are clear - to find, preserve and study the geniuses of the past within the borders of the district, as well as the creation of a museum. In May 1905, under the leadership of Yurdan Kantardzhiev, the society organized and carried out the first archaeological excavations at the \"Storgozia\" fortress in Kajlyka Park, near Pleven. Excavated materials for the Minaloto on Pleven allow the archaeological society to reveal in 1911 museum collection. After 1923 this activity continued under the leadership of the \"Saglasie\" reading room, where the collected materials were transferred and a museum was organized. But the most significant development of the museum work in Pleven is recorded after 1953. when the State General People's Museum of History was created. With Resolution No. 153 of the Council of Ministers of the Republic of Bulgaria dated July 1, 2000. the museum was transformed into the Regional Historical Museum - Pleven, with the scope of its activity on the territory of the Pleven and Loveška regions. Since 1984 The museum is located in a two-story building of impressive proportions with artistic-architectural and historical value - a symbol of culture with national significance, built in 1884-1888, according to the Italian project for the barracks. As a result of the long-term work and dedicated activity of more than three generations of museum workers, today RIM - Pleven is among the largest museums in Bulgaria with an impressive collection of over 180,000 items - documentary and artistic evidence for history, material and spiritual culture, and specimens from living and non-living nature, which are part of the national cultural-historical and natural heritage. It has a high artistic, historical and natural scientific value and is extremely valuable evidence not only for Bulgarian history and culture, but also for the paleontological and anthropological past of the town of Pleven and the region, but also for the history of different cultures and peoples, left a lasting mark on our country and in the European cultural space. Bulgaria. vascular plants, invertebrates, palaeobotany" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/90944dfa-0357-49f9-9c35-0c3183827461> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(24.617663 43.404352)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
