<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/44edbbe3-d912-44b9-b1e4-29a8440fd58d> <https://schema.org/description> "The natural history collections of Udine’s secondary schools and the city’s scientific cabinets (including those linked to historic institutions such as the Stellini Institute or the Zanon Institute) have played a fundamental role in the emergence and development of the local scientific heritage, with links to the origins of the MFSN, founded in the 19th century. There is no evidence that the institution in question holds scientific collections anymore." .

