<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/163cbdcb-5aca-4746-967a-6dd254c99a1f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/163cbdcb-5aca-4746-967a-6dd254c99a1f> <https://schema.org/name> "Museo de fauna Silvestre del Cantón Montúfar" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/163cbdcb-5aca-4746-967a-6dd254c99a1f> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "GADM" .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4f8530a9-9d35-4290-a4c4-ca446d0800a3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4f8530a9-9d35-4290-a4c4-ca446d0800a3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4f8530a9-9d35-4290-a4c4-ca446d0800a3> <https://schema.org/name> "Museo Rumiñahui" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4f8530a9-9d35-4290-a4c4-ca446d0800a3> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "MR" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4f8530a9-9d35-4290-a4c4-ca446d0800a3> <https://schema.org/description> "El museo tiene aproximadamente 40 años de existencia, empezó por la afición de Luis LaraÉl inició recopilando antigüedades, mientras trabajaba con sus padres en el campo. Eran ollas, utensilios, etc. El museo tiene 6 salas, en la primera hay lo referente a taxidermia, es decir, animales embalsamados o disecados, la mayoría endémicos como danta, tapir, ojo de anteojos, etc. En la segunda sala hay una biblioteca con más de 3.000 libros, algunos ejemplares tienen más de 500 años de antigüedad. En la tercera sala hay antigüedades como fonógrafos, rocolas, etc. La cuarta y quinta sala tienen utensilios antiguos, planchas de carbón, de gasolina. La sexta sala tiene vestigios de arqueología." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d4e731a5-38fc-4108-9bb7-f16f0ff55a91> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d4e731a5-38fc-4108-9bb7-f16f0ff55a91> <https://schema.org/name> "Fungario QCAM de la Pontificia Universidad Católica del Ecuador" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d4e731a5-38fc-4108-9bb7-f16f0ff55a91> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "QCAM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d4e731a5-38fc-4108-9bb7-f16f0ff55a91> <https://schema.org/description> "El Fungario QCAM es la colección más grande de macrohongos del Ecuador. Contamos con cerca de 7700 muestras ingresadas en la colección. El Fungario es una entidad que se dedica a la investigación científica, formación de investigadores, y a salvaguardar una parte importante de la diversidad biológica como referencia histórica y científica." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d4e731a5-38fc-4108-9bb7-f16f0ff55a91> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-78.49172 -0.21024)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/aba8fa5c-1e47-4d86-a93a-7f267784e478> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/aba8fa5c-1e47-4d86-a93a-7f267784e478> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/aba8fa5c-1e47-4d86-a93a-7f267784e478> <https://schema.org/name> "Museo Héctor Vásquez Salazar de la Unidad Educativa Bolivar" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/aba8fa5c-1e47-4d86-a93a-7f267784e478> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "MHVSUEB" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/aba8fa5c-1e47-4d86-a93a-7f267784e478> <https://schema.org/description> "El museo de la Unidad Educativa Bolívar es uno de los sitios más visitados en el centro de Ambato. Inicio sus servicios en el año de 1920 con 200 piezas de Zoología. Actualmente, cuenta con 8 secciones en las que se exhiben más de 7.000 objetos." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/aba8fa5c-1e47-4d86-a93a-7f267784e478> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-78.637342 -1.251627)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6c782bd1-8965-4911-8ae3-5849ff812d30> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6c782bd1-8965-4911-8ae3-5849ff812d30> <https://schema.org/name> "University of Santo Tomas Museum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6c782bd1-8965-4911-8ae3-5849ff812d30> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "USTM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6c782bd1-8965-4911-8ae3-5849ff812d30> <https://schema.org/description> "The University of Santo Tomas Museum, considered as the oldest existing museum in the Philippines, was formally established in 1869, to comply with the 1865 Reglamento de Segunda Enseñanza that required all first class colleges to have a Museo de Historia Natural. Originally located in Intramuros, the UST Museum was later transferred to its present site at the paraninfo of the UST Main Building, built in 1928 in the Sampaloc district of Manila. The great Director of the Museum was Rev. Fr. Casto de Elera, O.P. He was born in Majorca (Leon), Spain on July 1st 1852; arrived in the Philippines in 1875 and in 1881 started teaching at the University of Santo Tomas as professor of Natural History and Director of the Museum. He reclassified everything and started a system of intercommunication of data and exchange of specimens between UST and the best museums of the world. His main interest was the animal life of the Philippines. He organized field expeditions all over the Philippines to collect specimens. In the stocks of the Museum there are still many specimens, specially of very small, almost microscopic, shells, of butterflies, birds, etc. that have the field notes attached to them. A definite scientific work of his, and a catalogue at the same time of the animal specimens at the Museum of Santo Tomas is his monumental Catalogo Sistematico de Toda la Fauna de Filipinas Conocida Hasta el Presente y Alavez de la Coleccion Zoologica del Museo del Colegio Universidad de Sto. Tomas de Manila – Manila – UST – 1895. " .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6c782bd1-8965-4911-8ae3-5849ff812d30> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(120.987091 14.610177)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6c782bd1-8965-4911-8ae3-5849ff812d30> <https://schema.org/logo> <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/sitesv/AAzXCkdUbkmbk4bC84n-caDfs1UpvkjaJX54Wj0AGhnz7CwrPbL6xa59nKt7E93PBHGzc8e61q7H6Kp2ZnJa_2YovzuFFpc_hplYD0YJrXEPFJcC1Jc6kvGy9vcP-cFHPcO4ToV5yO7OOirAw4Mlxhm2zJZz4YCUfjpat_wIpjhDCdxqKtsGIPmbyjz0QBck4wg4n_gCaXctFxMSBFA=w1280> .

