<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/2bf4822a-6648-49f1-a26a-a6764349a503> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/2bf4822a-6648-49f1-a26a-a6764349a503> <https://schema.org/name> "Perkalsky Arboretum of the Komarov Botanical Institute" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/2bf4822a-6648-49f1-a26a-a6764349a503> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "PALE" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/2bf4822a-6648-49f1-a26a-a6764349a503> <https://schema.org/description> "The Perkalsky Dendrological Park is a subdivision of the V.L. Komarov Botanical Institute of the Russian Academy of Sciences (BIN RAN); a specially protected natural area of federal significance. The park is part of the Council of Botanical Gardens of Russia and the Regional Council of Botanical Gardens of Southern Russia. The Perkalsky Arboretum was established in 1879 on the northern slope of Mount Mashuk as a nursery for ornamental plants for the landscaping of public gardens in the Caucasian Mineral Waters region and the forests of the Beshtaugorskaya forest estate. In 2017, the Perkalsky Dendrological Park of the V.L. Komarov Botanical Institute of the Russian Academy of Sciences was established as a specially protected natural area of federal significance, based on the Ecological and Botanical Station \"Pyatigorsk.\"" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/2bf4822a-6648-49f1-a26a-a6764349a503> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(43.1 44.1)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

