<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/007324a5-6d2f-475b-a93e-e7d6ca774fb8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/007324a5-6d2f-475b-a93e-e7d6ca774fb8> <https://schema.org/name> "University of Santo Tomas - Zooplankton Ecology, Systematics, and Limnology Laboratory" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/007324a5-6d2f-475b-a93e-e7d6ca774fb8> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "UST-ZESL" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/007324a5-6d2f-475b-a93e-e7d6ca774fb8> <https://schema.org/description> "The Zooplankton Ecology, Systematics, and Limnology research group of the University of Santo Tomas Research Center for the Natural and Applied Sciences (UST-ZESL) was established in 2011 with the following core research objectives: (1) zooplankton studies focusing on taxonomy, distribution, and systematics of microcrustaceans, (2) spatio-temporal approach in studying zooplankton ecology as well as studies on zooplankton community dynamics and lake monitoring, (3) paleolimnology and time-series data, (4) taxonomy and life history of fish parasites, (5) freshwater ecology focusing on nutrient spiral metrics, trophic dynamics, and community structure, (6) organismic biology focusing on reproduction, development, and life history, (7) invasive and keystone species, and (8) applied freshwater research focusing on utilization of freshwater organisms as models, bioindicators, biomonitors, and biocontrol. The UST-ZESL is home to the first and only organized assemblage of zooplankton samples and specimens collected within the Philippines. The Philippine Zooplankton Reference Collection which was established in 2011 is an integral tool in documenting zooplankton diversity, distribution, and ecology in Philippine inland waters. The ZRC's main objectives is to develop a systematic way of organizing and documenting collections (unsorted and sorted wet samples and dissected specimens mounted on slides) and to develop a standardized process of studying zooplankton which involves sampling, processing, analysis, and molecular analysis (SPAM). Through the years, the collection has grown and is now home to at least a thousand sorted and unsorted samples and 727 zooplankton specimens mounted on slides." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/007324a5-6d2f-475b-a93e-e7d6ca774fb8> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/00d25af97> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/007324a5-6d2f-475b-a93e-e7d6ca774fb8> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(120.98958 14.60982)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/007324a5-6d2f-475b-a93e-e7d6ca774fb8> <https://schema.org/logo> <https://scontent.fmnl6-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/12391101_1245672958779996_7155372730339826569_n.jpg?_nc_cat=104&_nc_ht=scontent.fmnl6-2.fna&oh=9490a6eda7773a1bc228406356a05571&oe=5D1D4C2C> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e1666b1f-f017-4a8f-8d98-a675360bed6e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e1666b1f-f017-4a8f-8d98-a675360bed6e> <https://schema.org/name> "USDA Agricultural Research Service (ARS)" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e1666b1f-f017-4a8f-8d98-a675360bed6e> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "USDA-ARS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e1666b1f-f017-4a8f-8d98-a675360bed6e> <https://schema.org/description> "The Agricultural Research Service (ARS) is the chief in-house scientific research agency of the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA). Our job is finding solutions to agricultural problems that affect Americans every day from field to table. Our core values include scientific excellence, creativity, innovation, integrity, leadership, collaboration, accountability, transparency, diversity, respect, inclusiveness, and public service. These values underpin ARS' commitment to delivering cutting-edge, scientific tools and innovative solutions for American farmers, producers, industry, and communities to support the nourishment and well-being of all people; sustain our nation’s agroecosystems and natural resources; and ensure the economic competitiveness and excellence of our agriculture. Research stations and biological collections located across the United States and Puerto Rico. ARS' collections hold living and preserved specimens collected from all over the world. Animal, bacterial, fungal, and plant collections, as well as soil and geological samples." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e1666b1f-f017-4a8f-8d98-a675360bed6e> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/02d2m2044> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e1666b1f-f017-4a8f-8d98-a675360bed6e> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-76.908989 39.020351)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/60e918e7-a353-42e6-b995-da33e94238e0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/60e918e7-a353-42e6-b995-da33e94238e0> <https://schema.org/name> "USDA Animal and Plant Health Inspection Service (APHIS)" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/60e918e7-a353-42e6-b995-da33e94238e0> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "USDA-APHIS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/60e918e7-a353-42e6-b995-da33e94238e0> <https://schema.org/description> "APHIS protects the health and value of America's agricultural and natural resources. It’s a vital mission: Healthy and profitable American agriculture provides food and clothing for countless people worldwide and is a key pillar of our economy. Collections come from all around the world, mainly from interceptions of foreign material. Biological collections of animal and plant specimens." .
