<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/801cc29b-677e-41fc-ae40-040b80dd632c> <https://schema.org/name> "Institute of Tropical Biology" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/801cc29b-677e-41fc-ae40-040b80dd632c> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "ITBVAST" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/801cc29b-677e-41fc-ae40-040b80dd632c> <https://schema.org/description> "- Functions: Doing basic research, applying and developing technology in the scientific fields: Physiology, Biochemistry, Biotechnology, Ecology, Biological resources, Environment and Bio-active compounds. - Tasks: + Researching on basic and modern sciences in physiological, biochemical of plants, animals and microorganisms. + Studying many scientific - technological subjects which are in fields: Plant cell technology, Plant genetic engineering, Animal cell and embryo culture, Microbiology, Bioactive compounds technology, Bio conversion technology, Food technology and Technology for treatment of environment pollution. + Doing basic investigations and researches about problems in ecology, biological resources and environmental impact assessment. + Applying, deploying technologies and carrying out science and technology services related fields. + Joining in training cadres who research science and technology in biology. Organizing international cooperation in biological fields. + Managing staff, infrastructure and other properties of the institute. - Departments: + Department of Biological Resources + Department of Environmental Management & Technology + Department of Ecology + Department of Animal biotechnology + Department of Plant cell technology + Department of Gene technology + Department of Bio-conversion Technology + Department of Microbiology + Department of Bio-active Compounds + Museum of Flora and Fauna + National Key Laboratory of Plant cell technology - Units: + Administrative Department + Center of Application and Deployment of technology Human Resources - Total: 106 - Professors: 01 - Associate Professors: 04 - Doctors of Science: 01	- Doctors: 26 - Masters: 27 - Bachelors: 09 - Others: 01. Morphological and Genetical Taxonomy" .
