<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4e81ff61-cbe7-43c3-96a1-0082d97746cf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4e81ff61-cbe7-43c3-96a1-0082d97746cf> <https://schema.org/name> "SuanLuang Rama IX Royal Botanic Garden" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4e81ff61-cbe7-43c3-96a1-0082d97746cf> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "SLR" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4e81ff61-cbe7-43c3-96a1-0082d97746cf> <https://schema.org/description> "The concept and construction of Suan Luang Rama IX Royal Botanic Garden were a joint effort between the private and public sectors. Generous financial supports, in the form of donations, obtained from public all over the country. The Garden was established in honor of His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej on the auspicious occasion of 60th Birthday Anniversary in 1987 and His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej officially opened the Garden on December 1, 1987. Botanical Building (Herbarium) deposites preserved plant specimens and associated information used for scientific study. The specimens are on herbarium sheets or preserved in various forms for display. The herbarium, housing a botanical library, is opened for academic study and botanical research. The building also serves as an office for botanists and associated staff." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4e81ff61-cbe7-43c3-96a1-0082d97746cf> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(100.658989 13.688454)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9389bf5c-7e49-45f1-a748-92d502cff684> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9389bf5c-7e49-45f1-a748-92d502cff684> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9389bf5c-7e49-45f1-a748-92d502cff684> <https://schema.org/name> "Gyeryonsan Natural History Museum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9389bf5c-7e49-45f1-a748-92d502cff684> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "GNHM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9389bf5c-7e49-45f1-a748-92d502cff684> <https://schema.org/description> "Korean Natural History Museum is located at the foot of the Gyeryongsan National Park, famous for its beautiful natural landscape, and it is a famous landmark of education and experience that boasts the largest size and the largest collection in Korea. Our dynamic exhibits include the Dinosaur Hall, where real dinosaur fossils have been restored, Universe, Earth and Life, Rocks and Gems, World of Animals, World of the Ocean, World of Plants, World of Insects, Nature and Human Being Hall, and Mummy Hall, covering from the birth of the universe to present day, arousing the curiosity and the inquiring mind in children and adolescents to foster the dream of becoming a natural scientist." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9389bf5c-7e49-45f1-a748-92d502cff684> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(127.14001 36.469008)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/193e711e-a613-4bc5-860e-82098e9908fc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/193e711e-a613-4bc5-860e-82098e9908fc> <https://schema.org/name> "Industrial Technology Development Institute, Department of Science and Technology" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/193e711e-a613-4bc5-860e-82098e9908fc> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "ITDI" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/193e711e-a613-4bc5-860e-82098e9908fc> <https://schema.org/description> "The ITDI is among the instrumentalities that laid the groundwork, in the early years, for S&T in the country. Today, it is one of the DOST's RDIs (research and development institutes) and undertakes multidisciplinary industrial R&D, technical services, and knowledge translation or technology transfer and commercialization. ITDI harnesses know-how in new technology and product innovation, and through the years, has emerged as a credible and reliable industry and government partner in accelerating growth and development in the country." .
