<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/af8f20da-14c5-42c1-80b7-c0060dbd435c> <https://schema.org/name> "University of Leicester" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/af8f20da-14c5-42c1-80b7-c0060dbd435c> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "LTR" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/af8f20da-14c5-42c1-80b7-c0060dbd435c> <https://schema.org/description> "The University of Leicester holds many different types of , collections for teaching and learning purposes , at Higher Education level. Collections are also available for , research to interested parties both within the organisation and , externally., Collections falling under Natural Sciences remit, though held by different Schools and Departments across UoL, are, - geological & palaeontological & extraterrestrial (Geology), - herbarium , - animal bones (Archaeology), - carpological (Archaeology), , Note on the E.T. material: We do have physics & astronomy departments and Space Research who may well hold their own specimens, but status as to whether these are curated remains uncertain. Worldwide - certainly the case for the geological and , palaeontology collections" .
