<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/661b16d8-ff6f-4f6d-95d4-5faa6ff65da3> <https://schema.org/name> "The Powell-Cotton Museum, Quex House and Gardens" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/661b16d8-ff6f-4f6d-95d4-5faa6ff65da3> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "BICPC" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/661b16d8-ff6f-4f6d-95d4-5faa6ff65da3> <https://schema.org/description> "Museum of largely natural history and world cultures material. Originally a private museum of the Powell-Cotton family, now run as an independent charity. Located in Birchington, Kent, on the Powell-Cotton family estate, Quex Park. The Natural History collection largely comprises African mammals, including a large and an internationally important collection of primates. The majority of the Museum's holdings originate from across the African continent and Indian subcontinent, but we also hold some material from across Europe, East Asia, and Oceania. The archaeology collection largely comprises local material excavated in Kent." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/661b16d8-ff6f-4f6d-95d4-5faa6ff65da3> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/0596srd08> .
