<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a27138c0-a05b-44ed-bdb5-d57d4c135eb5> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "POOMS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a27138c0-a05b-44ed-bdb5-d57d4c135eb5> <https://schema.org/description> "Poole Museum is a local authority museum run by BCP Council (formerly Borough of Poole), located just off Poole Quay (cureent collections stores are located offsite). Our full collection is approximatly 60,000 - 80,000 objects and is split into a series of collections areas: Archaeology; Books; Ceramics; Coins ad Medals; Costume and Textiles; Decorative Art; Documents; Ephemera; Fine Art; Furniture; Maps and Plans; Maritime; Natural History; Pharmacy; Photography, Audio and Video; Social History; World Cultures. The museum now has a strict collecting policy - all items must be linked to Poole. Historically there was no policy and the collections' geographic origins extends worldwide. Our focuss is Fine Art with Poole links, Poole Pottery, Maritime Archaeology, Maritime History. Natural History is likley to be a new key focus of our work. We are part of the Wessex Museums partnership, a colloborative partnership between Wessex Museums (Charity), Dorset Museum, Salisbury Museum, Poole Museum and Wiltshire Mu.. Worldwide" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a27138c0-a05b-44ed-bdb5-d57d4c135eb5> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q7228623> .
