<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a8df8efa-30be-413d-b6a5-5713396b8409> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "ANHM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a8df8efa-30be-413d-b6a5-5713396b8409> <https://schema.org/description> "The Annapurna Natural History Museum was established by an American Peace Corps Volunteer, late Dorothy Mierow in 1965 within the Prithvi Narayan Campus premises for the campus’s use and the people of Pokhara and its surrounding areas. The collections in display here includes the geological and biological. The museum is also known as 'The Butterfly Museum' because of the collection of almost all of Nepal's butterfly species. Bhimkali Patan, Bagar, Pokhara, Nepal. Butterfly, Plants and other animals" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a8df8efa-30be-413d-b6a5-5713396b8409> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(83.99053 28.23966)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/63f54d10-9c83-4dc6-8dd3-bc837bb7e0dd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/63f54d10-9c83-4dc6-8dd3-bc837bb7e0dd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/63f54d10-9c83-4dc6-8dd3-bc837bb7e0dd> <https://schema.org/name> "International Mountain Museum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/63f54d10-9c83-4dc6-8dd3-bc837bb7e0dd> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "IMM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/63f54d10-9c83-4dc6-8dd3-bc837bb7e0dd> <https://schema.org/description> "The basic objective for its establishment was made to record, document and chronicle the past and present development of mountaineering activities in the world in general and to preserve the saga of the momentous feats in the history of mountaineering in the Himalayan peaks in particular. Pokhara, Nepal" .
