<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a2e69864-6644-47e8-b869-1b698dc0d3bc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a2e69864-6644-47e8-b869-1b698dc0d3bc> <https://schema.org/name> "Council for Scientific and Industrial Research-Food Research Institute" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a2e69864-6644-47e8-b869-1b698dc0d3bc> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "CSIR-FRI National Mushroom mycelium bank" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a2e69864-6644-47e8-b869-1b698dc0d3bc> <https://schema.org/description> "Food Research Institute (FRI) is one of the thirteen affiliate Institutes and Centres of the Council for Scientific and Industrial Research (CSIR). It was established by the Government of Ghana on 1st Oct. 1963. The Institute has three main sites; Okponglo South Legon Accra(Main office, laboratory and Processing); Pokuasi Amasaman District ( Pilot Processing of Root and tuber products) ; Josef Broz Tito Avenue Cantonments Accra (Offices and residential). These facilities are equipped with analytical laboratories for chemistry, microbiology and biochemistry toxicology and nutrition. It also has an engineering and maintenance workshop, a test kitchen, sensory evaluation and salt iodation laboratories. In addition, the Institute has a pilot processing plant equipped with operational wet and dry processing lines which also houses the sorghum malting and brewing unit. The Institute has established a Root and Tuber Processing and Demonstration plant at Pokuase, near Accra. It also has facilities for mycology studies and houses the National Mushroom Mycelium Bank at the Okponglo site, Accra. Fifteen of its analytical methods are accredited to ISO/IEC 17025:2005" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a2e69864-6644-47e8-b869-1b698dc0d3bc> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/03ad6kn10> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a2e69864-6644-47e8-b869-1b698dc0d3bc> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-0.179343 5.629779)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cf68b61e-a6e6-4483-a97b-1ad7eb21188b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cf68b61e-a6e6-4483-a97b-1ad7eb21188b> <https://schema.org/name> "Nordre Øyeren Bird Observatory" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cf68b61e-a6e6-4483-a97b-1ad7eb21188b> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "NOEF" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cf68b61e-a6e6-4483-a97b-1ad7eb21188b> <https://schema.org/description> "Nordre Øyeren Bird Observatory (Nordre Øyeren fuglestasjon; NØF) was founded in 1974. Bird registrations and ringing activity done by NØF members prior to this revealed important biological values in the area, which led to the establishment of the Nordre Øyeren nature reserve in 1975 and its recognition as a Ramsar site in 1985. Today NØF focuses on standardized registrations of wetland birds during spring and autumn migration and maintains a dataset of more than 40 years of continuous observations, dating back to the mid-1970s. Data from NØF's waterfowl and wader counts, as well as common field registrations, are now digitized and published." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cf68b61e-a6e6-4483-a97b-1ad7eb21188b> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q106653361> .
