<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3d7a4d47-c970-45ce-9c29-b09a6375a489> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3d7a4d47-c970-45ce-9c29-b09a6375a489> <https://schema.org/name> "Darder Natural History Museum of Banyoles" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3d7a4d47-c970-45ce-9c29-b09a6375a489> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "MDEIE" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3d7a4d47-c970-45ce-9c29-b09a6375a489> <https://schema.org/description> "Darder Museum of Banyoles was inaugurated on 22 October 1916. Originally, the specimens of the Museum came from the donation of the natural history collections of Francesc Darder Llimona to the town of Banyoles. The collection includes original pieces of dissected animals from around the world, pieces of anthropology, skulls, fetus, human skins, and educational materials related to the natural sciences. The museum's collection also grew up with donations of other people who offered some of their natural sciences collections or objects to the Museum. Nowadays, the Museum collection reaches approximately to 20,000 objects or specimens. Also, it includes different general type collections: botanical, fossils, minerals, insects, mollusks, skeletons and dissected animals. Museum center: Darder Museum is one of the oldest in the surrounding Girona region. Opened in 1916, underwent few changes until its complete renovation, which began in 2003. In 2007 opens its doors again, incorporating a part dedicated to explaining the phenomenon of the hydrological basin of Lake Banyoles. The building which houses the Museum Darder was built in the late nineteenth century, but now retains only three walls of that old municipal building, where there was the Post Office and the Municipal School. Museum Science Area: This comprises the Collections departments and the Documentation Centre, and all the activities undertaken by them, that is, conservation, description and study of the natural and documentary heritage of their resources. In fact, everything that goes on at the Museum would be pointless were it not for its fundamental, primary purpose which is to safeguard and preserve that heritage. The collections are kept in store and are preserved and studied by biologists and geologists who document them (taking inventory, cataloging, computerizing, and publishing databases) and make them available for the scientific community. The Documentation Centre places the information resources it administers at the disposal of the Museum experts and the public." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3d7a4d47-c970-45ce-9c29-b09a6375a489> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(2.76502 42.1191)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3d7a4d47-c970-45ce-9c29-b09a6375a489> <https://schema.org/logo> <http://www.banyolescultura.net/capdarder.png> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c705c732-157f-404b-aa19-47ffccca2fd3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c705c732-157f-404b-aa19-47ffccca2fd3> <https://schema.org/name> "Ájtte Museum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c705c732-157f-404b-aa19-47ffccca2fd3> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "AJTT" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c705c732-157f-404b-aa19-47ffccca2fd3> <https://schema.org/description> "Ájtte, the Swedish Mountain and Sami Museum provides a gateway to the high mountains, to Laponia and to the Sami culture. Ájtte tells the story of Sápmi, the land and the people, of life and survival in a demanding climate and environment. Apart from preserving and presenting cultural artifacts Ájtte´s natural history collections comprise mammals, birds, fish, insects, other invertebrates, fungi, mosses, lichens and vascular plants. The primary objective of the collections is to preserve representative reference specimens of mammals and birds." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c705c732-157f-404b-aa19-47ffccca2fd3> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/01mvvkn82> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c705c732-157f-404b-aa19-47ffccca2fd3> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q250468> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c705c732-157f-404b-aa19-47ffccca2fd3> <https://schema.org/logo> <https://fbcdn-profile-a.akamaihd.net/hprofile-ak-ash2/276441_241581315887656_732411485_q.jpg> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b3dd05dc-3a3f-4ad9-9b13-158f7bab274c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b3dd05dc-3a3f-4ad9-9b13-158f7bab274c> <https://schema.org/name> "Arkansas Archeological Survey" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b3dd05dc-3a3f-4ad9-9b13-158f7bab274c> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "ARAS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b3dd05dc-3a3f-4ad9-9b13-158f7bab274c> <https://schema.org/description> "The mission of the Arkansas Archeological Survey is to study Arkansas' past, to preserve and manage information about archeological sites, and to share what we learn with the people of Arkansas. We invite members of the public to help discover and record information about archeological sites in Arkansas. Its collections include archeological, ethnographic, zooarchaeological, ethnobotanical, archaeobotanical and archaeometric collections. ARAS is also charged with maintaining georeferenced records for all archaeological sites and cultural resources in the state. The Arkansas Archeological Survey is a state-chartered agency formally charged with maintaining georeferenced records for all archaeological site sand cultural resources within the state of Arkansas. Archaeological remains including artifacts, scientific samples, and zoological, botanical and geoarchaeological materials related to those sites, as well as records of geophysical and other remote sensing records of sites and cultural landscapes" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b3dd05dc-3a3f-4ad9-9b13-158f7bab274c> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-94.17959 36.096759)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7d014689-22c7-497b-9201-21088c802c31> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7d014689-22c7-497b-9201-21088c802c31> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7d014689-22c7-497b-9201-21088c802c31> <https://schema.org/name> "Museo de Zoología, Universidad Técnica Particular de Loja" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7d014689-22c7-497b-9201-21088c802c31> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "MUTPL" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7d014689-22c7-497b-9201-21088c802c31> <https://schema.org/description> "Museo de Zoología houses the zoological collections of the Universidad Técnica Particular de Loja, Ecuador, and include both invertebrate (especially Insecta and Araneae) and vertebrate collections (Ichthyology, Herpetology, Ornithology and Mammalogy Collections).The services provided by MUTPL are as follows: storage of specimens, sample processing, identification of specimens, consultation of collections and databases, research advice and support, issuance of certificates and loans of specimens.Currently in the Universidad Técnica Particular de Loja the Museum of Zoology leads the scientific processes in the field of systematic zoology especially the collection, identification, systematization and phylogenetic studies of invertebrates, amphibians, reptiles and mammals of southern Ecuador. Southern Ecuador" .
