<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/273740a1-edac-49bb-a5b9-96f5c8e4d32a> <https://schema.org/description> "The Natural History Society of Maryland (NHSM) was established in 1929 when a group of men interested in the natural sciences broke away from the Maryland Academy of Sciences and formed the NHSM. In 1936, the Society established a ‘Maryland Natural History Museum’ at Druid Hill Park in Baltimore City. This was a display museum open to the public. The NHSM started a new chapter in its history in 2006 with the purchase of a 9,000-square-foot building at 6908 Belair Road in Overlea, Baltimore County. The NHSM collections include items collected by Marylanders in the disciplines of geology, mineralogy, entomology, malacology, herpetology, ornithology, mammalogy, paleontology, anthropology and botany." .
