<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e3295a7c-5a23-41a9-a99a-eb16540571a8> <https://schema.org/name> "University of Jammu" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e3295a7c-5a23-41a9-a99a-eb16540571a8> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "HBJU" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e3295a7c-5a23-41a9-a99a-eb16540571a8> <https://schema.org/description> "The University of Jammu strives for Achieving world-class excellence in teaching, research and knowledge transfer and making valuable contributions to the socioeconomic development of the region and country. Department of Botany, University of Jammu is having the herbarium facility where the more than 17000 specimen of plants (angiosperms, gymnosperms, pteridophytes, bryophytes, macrofungi and algae) are preserved, either in dry form on herbarium sheets or in preservative jars. In addition, seed samples and other plant originated artefacts are also preserved in the museum. . Mostly the specimens in the herbarium are Himalayan plants collected from NW Himalaya. . Herbarium consists of specimens from angiosperms, gymnosperms, pteridophytes, bryophytes and mushrooms. " .
