<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/135e8acf-d618-4203-8fca-631d044a9d55> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/135e8acf-d618-4203-8fca-631d044a9d55> <https://schema.org/name> "Verde Island Passage Center for Oceanographic Research and Aquatic Life Sciences" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/135e8acf-d618-4203-8fca-631d044a9d55> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "VIP CORALS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/135e8acf-d618-4203-8fca-631d044a9d55> <https://schema.org/description> "The Verde Island Passage Center for Oceanographic Research and Aquatic Life Sciences (VIP Corals) at Batangas State University – The National Engineering University was established in February 2018, following approval by the University’s Board of Regents through Resolution No. 004, Series of 2018. The research center operates from its current office located at VIP Corals BL1, BL2 (2nd Floor) and Room 402 (4th Floor) of the CIRTC Building, within Batangas State University – Pablo Borbon Campus, situated on Rizal Avenue Extension, Batangas City, Philippines. Additionally, it maintains the Lobo Marine Station at Batangas State University – Lobo Campus, located in Brgy. Masaguitsit, Lobo, Batangas (13°38′30′′N, 121°11′33′′E). The center envisions becoming a pioneer, leading, proactive, and world-class research facility in the field of oceanographic research and aquatic life sciences within the Verde Island Passage. Its general mandate is to provide research, teaching, and extension services focused on marine resources and the marine environment of the Verde Island Passage, in alignment with Batangas State University’s mission and goals." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/135e8acf-d618-4203-8fca-631d044a9d55> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(121.074386 13.784324)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
