<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/082e7ee2-5c51-4fa8-9a11-fa51b8cec5e2> <https://schema.org/description> "The State University of New York at Oswego is a public institution serving 6,000 undergraduates and 1,000 graduate students from its campus on the shores of Lake Ontario. The institution's herbarium houses specimens from all continents except Antarctica. The institution also houses non-digitized animal and invertebrate collections primarily from eastern North America, concentrated around Central New York and Lake Ontario. Plant collection (digitized) Animal and invertebrate collections (not digitized)" .
