<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/cef268e8-198e-4b76-88a8-47e34fa45d48> <https://schema.org/description> "Mazhar Botanic Garden is a nonprofit botanical garden in Egypt, located in the Barageel district of the Giza governorate, 5 km away from central Cairo. Mazhar Botanic Garden began in the fifties as a garden for collecting various fruits & roses but gradually it turned to a live collection of all kinds of plants, including palms, trees, shrubs, bamboo, cactus, bulbs, ferns and aquatic plants." .
