<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/63b5eefd-1fde-4866-a4a0-a788dccd6db5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/63b5eefd-1fde-4866-a4a0-a788dccd6db5> <https://schema.org/name> "Biodiversity Application & Research Center, Atatürk University" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/63b5eefd-1fde-4866-a4a0-a788dccd6db5> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "ABBM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/63b5eefd-1fde-4866-a4a0-a788dccd6db5> <https://schema.org/description> "Biodiversity Application & Research Center of Atatürk University was established at 11 May 2018, formally. The main task of this research center is to develop “Biodiversity Science Museum” of Atatürk University. " .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/875e914a-1b4c-4451-9eb4-267b6138e6ed> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/875e914a-1b4c-4451-9eb4-267b6138e6ed> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/875e914a-1b4c-4451-9eb4-267b6138e6ed> <https://schema.org/name> "Lingnan University Natural History Museum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/875e914a-1b4c-4451-9eb4-267b6138e6ed> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "LINGU" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/875e914a-1b4c-4451-9eb4-267b6138e6ed> <https://schema.org/description> "The Lingnan University Natural History Museum (LINGU) is a natural history museum at Lingnan University, Hong Kong. The museum was established in 2019 to document and preserve the living organisms of Hong Kong, starting with amphibians and reptiles (funded by the Environment and Conservation Fund, Hong Kong Government). In addition to traditional specimens, the LINGU collection includes tissue samples, photographs, and field notes. The collection started in 2019 to contribute to the goals of Hong Kong's Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan (BSAP) and it is funded by The Environment and Conservation Fund (ECF) from the Hong Kong Government (ECF 86/2081). Our first goal is to document the herpetological diversity across Hong Kong, and to become an important resource for research, conservation, and education. The collection includes: 1) specimens preserved in ethanol, 2) images of live and preserved specimens, and 3) tissue samples preserved in ethanol and RNA later." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/875e914a-1b4c-4451-9eb4-267b6138e6ed> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1541161> .
