<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7a717903-d4c7-4a83-a0cb-aaaca212228e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7a717903-d4c7-4a83-a0cb-aaaca212228e> <https://schema.org/name> "NSF Ice Core Facility" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7a717903-d4c7-4a83-a0cb-aaaca212228e> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "NSFICF" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7a717903-d4c7-4a83-a0cb-aaaca212228e> <https://schema.org/description> "The National Science Foundation Ice Core Facility (NSF-ICF) is the nation’s repository for storing, curating, and studying ice cores recovered from ice sheets, ice caps, and glaciers of the world, predominately from Antarctica and Greenland. The NSF-ICF facility provides the ice core community with the capability to conduct examination and measurements on ice cores while preserving the integrity of these cores in a safeguarded temperature-controlled environment for current and future investigations. The NSF-ICF is open to the public Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. The NSF-ICF gives tours by appointment, sign up. on the website- icecores.org. Ice Cores stored at -36°C" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/7a717903-d4c7-4a83-a0cb-aaaca212228e> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/05sk14837> .

