<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/def5b78b-7b82-4a4b-9bdc-ae7c9f84ffea> <https://schema.org/name> "HHS/CDC, National Center for Health Statistics" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/def5b78b-7b82-4a4b-9bdc-ae7c9f84ffea> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "CDC-NCHS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/def5b78b-7b82-4a4b-9bdc-ae7c9f84ffea> <https://schema.org/description> "NCHS refers to the National Health and Nutrition Exanination Surveys (NHANES). Serum samples are avaible from participants from this population based surveys from years 1999-2012." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ca6185e2-5f9f-4695-a2f9-7cd5c19cb690> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ca6185e2-5f9f-4695-a2f9-7cd5c19cb690> <https://schema.org/name> "Department of Veterans Affairs" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ca6185e2-5f9f-4695-a2f9-7cd5c19cb690> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "VA" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ca6185e2-5f9f-4695-a2f9-7cd5c19cb690> <https://schema.org/description> "The Veterans Health Administration is a large healthcare system encompassing over 150 medical centers across the country. As a part of VHA, the Office of Research &amp; Development strives to improve the healthcare of Veterans. ****Please contact people specific to each institutional collection where it may reside. For example, the Veteran Affairs Biorepository Brain Bank for ALS is located in Tucson, Arizona****" .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/874ed64b-68f6-421a-a03b-5e64e67388a9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/874ed64b-68f6-421a-a03b-5e64e67388a9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/874ed64b-68f6-421a-a03b-5e64e67388a9> <https://schema.org/name> "Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Natural History Museum (PSU Museum, Prince of Songkla University, Thailand)" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/874ed64b-68f6-421a-a03b-5e64e67388a9> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "PSUZC" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/874ed64b-68f6-421a-a03b-5e64e67388a9> <https://schema.org/description> "Faculty of Science by the biology department have started collecting and collecting samples of living things, both plants and animals from the students field study The samples collected were used for teaching and learning. In addition, some samples were brought to the exhibition for interested parties to view the collection. Plant specimens have developed systematically before. and established as a plant museum of the department It was later registered as an international plant museum, which is one of the four plants museums in Thailand that are registered as international plant museums. Currently, plant specimens are collected, especially plants. In Thailand, approximately 30,000 samples of animal specimens have been collected in large numbers. and stored as a system for reference studies Subsequently, the Department of Biology began There are additional exhibitions on the evolution of nature studies. and geology, which the Department of Mining Engineering and Metallurgy has presented examples on display. The Faculty of Science recognizes the importance of the Natural History Museum. Therefore, it has been upgraded to be an independent agency directly up to the Faculty of Science. Thailand, especially the peninsula." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/874ed64b-68f6-421a-a03b-5e64e67388a9> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(100.49726 7.00779)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/874ed64b-68f6-421a-a03b-5e64e67388a9> <https://schema.org/logo> <https://nhm.psu.ac.th/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/psunhm-logo.png> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/74884348-0703-4db6-ab49-b378218f5ae5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/74884348-0703-4db6-ab49-b378218f5ae5> <https://schema.org/name> "Centro Jambatu de Investigación y Conservación de Anfibios, Fundación Jambatu" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/74884348-0703-4db6-ab49-b378218f5ae5> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "CJ" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/74884348-0703-4db6-ab49-b378218f5ae5> <https://schema.org/description> "Nuestra misión es investigar y ejecutar el Plan de acción para la conservación de los anfibios de Ecuador. Nuestros objetivos son los de generar nuevos conocimientos y conceptos sobre los anfibios, y por esa vía desarrollar tecnologías e implementar un \"Arca de Noé\" moderna con ranas a bordo y la participación de científicos, conservacionistas, educadores, comunicadores y comunidad, diseñada para mitigar y prevenir la disminución y extinción de los anfibios. Nuestras investigaciones cubren un amplio rango de ramas de la ciencia; entre ellas la taxonomía, morfología, evolución, biogeografía, historia natural, comportaminento, reproducción, declive de los anfibios, entre otras. Nuestra actividad de conservación se enmarca en una actitud proactiva –en lugar de reactiva o post-mortem— para enfrentar y mitigar las tradicionales y las nuevas amenazas a la existencia de ranas, sapos, salamandras e ilulos. Entre estas últimas amenazas se cuentan el cambio climático y patógenos oportunistas. Nuestro accionar se enmarca en los principios de la bioética (autonomía, beneficencia, no maleficencia, justicia) y practicamos valores de integridad, honradez, responsabilidad, transparencia, pasión, equidad, optimismo, y solidaridad. Con estos principios y valores fomentamos la generación de bioconocimiento para el Buen Vivir." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/74884348-0703-4db6-ab49-b378218f5ae5> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-78.460434 -0.296597)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/74884348-0703-4db6-ab49-b378218f5ae5> <https://schema.org/logo> <http://www.anfibiosecuador.ec/imagenes/logoCJ.png> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c420c6b9-92d8-488b-b146-d5757005a604> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c420c6b9-92d8-488b-b146-d5757005a604> <https://schema.org/name> "CENTRE DE RESSOURCES DE VAILHAN" .
