<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/2d73e13c-947a-4dbc-980a-9ca592374831> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "ILRI" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/2d73e13c-947a-4dbc-980a-9ca592374831> <https://schema.org/description> "Azizi Biorepository is the long term storage system and associated informatics tools that comprise the biorepository at http://ilri.org." .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b0a98fde-b017-4e87-a997-e6452bb11bd6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b0a98fde-b017-4e87-a997-e6452bb11bd6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b0a98fde-b017-4e87-a997-e6452bb11bd6> <https://schema.org/name> "Natural History Institute" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b0a98fde-b017-4e87-a997-e6452bb11bd6> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "NHI" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b0a98fde-b017-4e87-a997-e6452bb11bd6> <https://schema.org/description> "The Natural History Institute at Prescott College began their collections in January 2014. These collections focus on plant and insect specimens from the Mogollon Highlands of Central Arizona. Currently, they house about 9,000 herbarium specimens, most of which were transfered from the Yavapai College Herbarium, along with 172 bird study skins, also donated by Yavapai College, and about 600 pinned insects. Eventually, data will be made available through SEINet and SCAN." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/b0a98fde-b017-4e87-a997-e6452bb11bd6> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-112.467648 34.542842)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

