<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a1059112-b0bb-4837-a151-9afdc77ef81f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a1059112-b0bb-4837-a151-9afdc77ef81f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a1059112-b0bb-4837-a151-9afdc77ef81f> <https://schema.org/name> "University of Texas at Austin" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a1059112-b0bb-4837-a151-9afdc77ef81f> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "NPL" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a1059112-b0bb-4837-a151-9afdc77ef81f> <https://schema.org/description> "The Non-vertebrate Paleontology Laboratory (NPL) was founded in 1999 to provide a unified hub for the development of this vast repository of over 4 million specimens. Our holdings include 22,000 type and figured specimens, historic collections from the early Geological Surveys of the State of Texas and sizable contributions from the ongoing studies of NPL research fellows. Areas of Emphasis: Chronostratographic- Paleozoic, Cretaceous and Paleogene/Neogene material. Taxonomic- echinoderms, brachiopods, molluscs, corals and sponges. Geographic- about 60% of the collection derive from Texas, with substantial holdings from Mexico, Europe and Australia." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a1059112-b0bb-4837-a151-9afdc77ef81f> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q49213> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/1616f171-9f72-4114-be87-58399550879c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/1616f171-9f72-4114-be87-58399550879c> <https://schema.org/name> "Neuromarker Resource Bank" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/1616f171-9f72-4114-be87-58399550879c> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "NRB" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/1616f171-9f72-4114-be87-58399550879c> <https://schema.org/description> "Neuromarker Resource Bank (NRB) at the Laboratory of Animal Research ASAN Medical Center and University of Ulsan College of Medicine was established for collection and distribution of neural cell type specific specimen The NRB is a central resource bank for experimentally validated mouse non-coding DNA with gene enhancer activity as confirmed in transgenic mice. The information of resources created by transgenic technique is available to the scientific community through this public website. The NRB also distributes various BAC, cDNA and total RNA, Protein, genomic DNA sampled from mouse brain." .

