<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/284e3ed7-92fb-4d31-b85b-a9b8062ed091> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated Mar 2013 (general upate). NOTE: Please address shipments to the relevant curator (see Correspondents) rather than to \"Herbarium.\" Five private herbaria are stored at KRAM. Other web addresses: http://botan.ib-pan.krakow.pl/. An additional series published by KRAM is Polish Botanical Guidebooks. ALGAE (408000 icons of 55000 taxa) worldwide, especially Europe; BRYOPHYTES (205000 specimens) worldwide, especially Poland, Europe, Africa, S America, Antarctica, Subantarctica (S Georgia, Prince Edward Islands, Iles Crozet, Iles Kerguelen, Heard Island, Macquarie Island); FOSSILS (115000 specimens) mainly of Central and E Europe and W Antarctica, slides of pollen and spores worldwide; FUNGI (59000 specimens) mainly of Central Europe, Asia and Africa; LICHENES (70000 specimens) worldwide, especially Central Europe (Poland), S America (Bolivia, Peru), N America and Asia ( Mongolia, Kirgizstan, Siberia); MYXOMYCETES (1500 specimens) worldwide; VASCULAR PLANTS (722000 specimens) worldwide, especially Central European mountains." .
