<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3b68c25c-01ac-4665-8890-6dd3d2cf7daa> <https://schema.org/name> "White Sands National Monument" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3b68c25c-01ac-4665-8890-6dd3d2cf7daa> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "WSNM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3b68c25c-01ac-4665-8890-6dd3d2cf7daa> <https://schema.org/description> "Rising from the heart of the Tularosa Basin is one of the world's great natural wonders - the glistening white sands of New Mexico. Great wave-like dunes of gypsum sand have engulfed 275 square miles of desert, creating the world's largest gypsum dunefield. White Sands National Park preserves a major portion of this unique dunefield, along with the plants and animals that live here." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/3b68c25c-01ac-4665-8890-6dd3d2cf7daa> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1200164> .

