<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/81a4e265-2df7-4aa0-8bf3-cfb91edfa475> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "UMZM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/81a4e265-2df7-4aa0-8bf3-cfb91edfa475> <https://schema.org/description> "The University of Montana Philip L. Wright Zoological Museum (UMZM) is a research museum housing over 20,000 specimens of birds and mammals. It has an excellent representation of vertebrate biodiversity in the Northern Rocky Mountains, as well as some unique special collections from across the world. In addition to study skins and skeletal material, the museum has a growing number of tissues and photographs." .
