<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/34ad57e4-c9a5-4929-b433-b7bdc037758f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/34ad57e4-c9a5-4929-b433-b7bdc037758f> <https://schema.org/name> "Department of Zoology, GC University" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/34ad57e4-c9a5-4929-b433-b7bdc037758f> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "GCU" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/34ad57e4-c9a5-4929-b433-b7bdc037758f> <https://schema.org/description> "The museum gradually grew and at presents it possess approximately 6000 specimens housed in a large hall in Zoology department, GC University, Lahore. The museum was named “Stephenson Natural History Museum” in 2004 after the name of the first chairperson of the department of Zoology, Dr.John Stephenson The natural history museum holds a unique place as it was amongst the first natural history museum to be established in South East Asia. A large number of specimens here provide a good opportunity for the study of biodiversity. In addition, the museum have some special unique specimens like a marvelous collection of butterflies, a toy terrier puppy, double headed calf, double headed chick, three legged hen, flying lizard, vertebrate eggs and much more to see. Our museum is of particular interest for the scientists, such as taxonomists, ecologists and evolutionary biologists. \"Type specimens\" of some local fish species have also been submitted here by the scientists. Comprehensive collection of birds, amphibian, reptiles, fishes and mammals makes our museum a place worth to visit. Also, a separate section has been allocated to invertebrate fauna and also for fossils collected from all over Pakistan." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/34ad57e4-c9a5-4929-b433-b7bdc037758f> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(74.307858 31.573417)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

