<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6d9125c9-fc20-4b54-a82b-ee9dcd08d78c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6d9125c9-fc20-4b54-a82b-ee9dcd08d78c> <https://schema.org/name> "Dinosaur Isle Museum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6d9125c9-fc20-4b54-a82b-ee9dcd08d78c> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "IWCMS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6d9125c9-fc20-4b54-a82b-ee9dcd08d78c> <https://schema.org/description> "Dinosaur Isle is a part of the Isle of Wight Council Museums Service, located at Sandown on the Isle of Wight. It is the current building for the Isle of Wight Geological Collection founded in 1820, and most recently previously located at the Museum of Isle of Wight Geology, Sandown, established 1914. It collects and preserves fossils and other geological materials from the Isle of Wight, and comparative material of relevance to the wider context of the Island's geological heritage. The collection's strengths are Wealden dinosaurs and associated fauna and flora, Paleogene molluscs, insects and vertebrates, and Cretaceous invertebrates and vertebrates.Research activities focus on Wealden dinosaurs, Wealden molluscs and late Eocene and early Oligocene molluscs. The museum holds type dinosaurs, pterosaurs, turtles, molluscs and insects, and many other status specimens. Isle of Wight, England" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6d9125c9-fc20-4b54-a82b-ee9dcd08d78c> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-1.141551 50.659866)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

