<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/70b18cea-8fba-41ac-94e2-f04b9640a2a5> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "BFUS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/70b18cea-8fba-41ac-94e2-f04b9640a2a5> <https://schema.org/description> "The university has several collection hosted at the different faculties and the botanical gardens: - - Faculty of Biology: herbarium, a living algal collection and a zoological collection - - Faculty of Geology: Paleontological collections of the Museum of the Paleontology - - Living plant collections of the three University Botanical Gardens. For more details see the page of each collection. algae, plants, lichens, inverterates (aphids, ants, plant- and leafhoppers, beetles, butterflies, nematodes, freshwater and sea crustaceans), and vertebrates (fishes and other vertebrates)." .
