<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/9e37bf7c-0304-4477-b506-e26fa6d5cf45> <https://schema.org/description> "organised into taxon-based departmental collectiions: 1. Plant collections in Botany Department also referred to as East African Herbarium 2. Mammals Collections in mammalogy Section 3. Fish Collections in Ichthyology Section 4. Amphibian and Reptile Collections in Herpetology Section 5. Birds collections in Ornithology Section 6. Invertebrate collections in Invertebrate Zoology Sections 7. Fossils of vertebrate collections in Paleontology Section 8. Fossil pollen collections in Palynology Section 9. assorted animal and pant collections in Exhibition galleries spread in several satelite Museum campuses in the country. Mainly eastern Africa (Ethiopia, Kenya, Tanzania, Uganda, Somalia) plus other African countries; mostly vascular plants, some bryophytes, fungi, and algae. Fungi (including lichens), Bryophytes, vascular plants" .
