<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d8687253-8ed2-48d0-9436-2a3cc7e1e98d> <https://schema.org/name> "I.I. Schmalhausen Institute of Zoology" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d8687253-8ed2-48d0-9436-2a3cc7e1e98d> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "SIZK" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/d8687253-8ed2-48d0-9436-2a3cc7e1e98d> <https://schema.org/description> "The I.I. Schmalhausen Institute of Zoology of the National Academy of Sciences of Ukraine is the oldest institution in Ukraine specialising in general zoology. Zoological researches within the Ukrainian Academy of Sciences have been started from the very beginning of its existence, in 1919, with the organisation of the \"Committee for Studies of the Fauna of Ukraine\" headed by M.F. Kaschenko. The Committee initiated the establishment of the Zoological Museum in May 1919. The Institute was founded in 1930 with Ivan I. Schmalhausen as its first director. At present 117 scientists work at the Institute, including two Corresponding Members of the NAS (V.A. Korneyev and A.V. Gumovsky), 18 Doctors of Science and 68 Doctors of Philosophy. SIZK is one of the largest repositories of zoological collections, currently containing over 60 million specimens." .
