<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f27fcee3-2258-4ac3-889a-a78d4ef3c23c> <https://schema.org/name> "Museo di Storia Naturale dell'Accademia dei Fisiocritici" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f27fcee3-2258-4ac3-889a-a78d4ef3c23c> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "MFS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f27fcee3-2258-4ac3-889a-a78d4ef3c23c> <https://schema.org/description> "The Museo di Storia Naturale dell’Accademia dei Fisiocritici is one of the oldest natural history museums in Italy, dedicated to the study, conservation, and dissemination of scientific knowledge. The museum holds extensive collections of zoological, botanical, geological, and paleontological specimens, with a strong focus on regional and Mediterranean biodiversity. Through its research activities, the museum contributes to the study of species distribution, taxonomy, and environmental changes, supporting biodiversity conservation efforts. The institution actively engages in citizen science projects, such as Siena BiodiverCity, promoting the collection and open sharing of biodiversity data to enhance scientific knowledge and public awareness." .
