<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f7a73987-a389-406f-84eb-bc5a0ca35835> <https://schema.org/description> "MUSE - Museo delle Scienze of Trento was founded in 1922. The museum is a public institution of the Autonomous Province of Trento and is one of the main Italian hubs of the scientific culture. Its archaeological and natural history collections house 5 millions specimens. MUSE develops projects of research, conservation, education, training and participation, mainly focused on the relationship among nature, science and society. Its mission is to interpret nature, starting with the mountain landscape, using the eyes, tools and questions of scientific research, picking up contemporary challenges and enjoying the pleasure of knowledge, to lend value to discovery, innovation, and sustainability." .
