<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f37de22d-3ee9-4e08-a3bd-b492f595a71f> <https://schema.org/description> "Leland Stanford Junior University, or Stanford University, is a private university in Stanford, California. The university was founded in 1885 by California senator Leland Stanford and his wife Jane Stanford. Much of Stanford's natural history collections were transferred to other institutions such as the California Academy of Sciences from the 1960s - 1980s. Today, Stanford's natural history collections include those of Hopkins Marine Station, Jasper Ridge Biological Preserve, the Stanford University Archeology Center, and geological and environmental samples held in the Doerr School of Sustainability Specimen Collections. The collections are global in scope." .
