<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a1f7ebc3-2980-489e-a0ba-ad0e6fe902f2> <https://schema.org/description> " The Port Elizabeth Museum is situated in Port Elizabeth, South Africa which forms part of the larger Bayworld Complex and is one of the oldest museums in South Africa (established in 1856). Our natural history research focus mainly on Marine Mammalogy, Marine Biology and Herpetology. We actively growing these collections by collecting new material and receiving donations across Africa and our offshore islands. Each collection in it's own is internationally recognised for its importance." .
