<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ae1380be-d358-4a85-a5ff-8a527908a96e> <https://schema.org/description> "The Cornell University Insect Collection is a world class research and training collection that includes over 7 million insects specimens representing about 200,000 species, or roughly 20% of the World&#39;s described insect fauna. Our collection is an important resource for Cornell students, staff and faculty, for the College of Agriculture, for residents of New York State, and for the broader systematics community." .

