<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/dfb4b730-641c-4a23-a524-df0f5afae7db> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/dfb4b730-641c-4a23-a524-df0f5afae7db> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/dfb4b730-641c-4a23-a524-df0f5afae7db> <https://schema.org/name> "Lee Kong Chian Natural History Museum, Faculty of Science, National University of Singapore, Singapore" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/dfb4b730-641c-4a23-a524-df0f5afae7db> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "LKCNHM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/dfb4b730-641c-4a23-a524-df0f5afae7db> <https://schema.org/description> "Lee Kong Chian Natural History Museum houses zoological and botanical specimens collected primarily in Singapore and Southeast Asia. The museum engages in biodiversity research with a Southeast Asian focus and aims to accelerate specimen-based research in this region. The museum is also heavily invested in public outreach activities to showcase the flora and fauna of this mega diverse region. Zoological collections are primarily focused on Southeast Asian specimens. Botanical collection focused on flora specimens from Singapore and Malaysia. Primary collections focused the following sections: Annelids, Birds, Corals and Sponges, Crustaceans, Echinoderms, Insects & other Terrestrial Arthropods, Fishes, Fish parasites, Reptiles & Amphibians, Mammals, Molluscs, Zooplankton. Botanical collections primarily focused on vascular and bryophyte flora" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/dfb4b730-641c-4a23-a524-df0f5afae7db> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(103.773624 1.30143)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
