<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/773a0d99-3ea8-4a8b-9191-accbdb47b4d3> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "ZMH" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/773a0d99-3ea8-4a8b-9191-accbdb47b4d3> <https://schema.org/description> "Museum of Nature in Hamburg is one part of the LIB - Leibniz Institute for the Analysis of Biodiversity Change (https://leibniz-lib.de). It is one of the most important natural-history-research museums in Germany. The ZMH has earned its high national and international reputation owing to its collection and research output. The collection as the heart of the museum includes approximately 10 million zoological objects and therefore forms the fourth largest of its kind in Germany." .
