<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/a9ab29d6-f380-4193-967f-15a64abc09e7> <https://schema.org/description> "The University of Oslo was founded in 1811 as the first in Norway. Located mainly on Blindern Campus in the northern part of Oslo, UiO has eight faculties: Faculty of Medicine; Faculty of Dentistry; Faculty of Law; Faculty of Theology; Faculty of Humanities; Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences; Faculty of Social Sciences; Faculty of Education Sciences. The capital university is also home to the Viking Ship Museum, the Historical Museum, and the Natural History Museum, a Main Library with 3.6 million holdings and a wide range of associated units and centres. All groups" .
