<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/daaa19c0-8ede-489b-802b-a5d54a14fb50> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/daaa19c0-8ede-489b-802b-a5d54a14fb50> <https://schema.org/name> "Institute of Food Research and Product Development, Kasetsart University" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/daaa19c0-8ede-489b-802b-a5d54a14fb50> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "IFRPD" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/daaa19c0-8ede-489b-802b-a5d54a14fb50> <https://schema.org/description> "Back then, Institute of Food Research and Product Development (IFRPD) was the Department of Education, Experiment, and Research of the Ready Meal Production Agency - a governmental organization responsible for providing machines and tools for food production and experiment to Thai army in 1955. It was located in the areas of Kasesart University and the head of the said department was Professor Amara Bhumiratana. Later, the Ready Meal Production Agency established a large factory at Ban Pong, Ratchaburi. The Department of Education, Experiment, and Research, therefore, had no longer needed. The cabinet at that time, then, decided to transfer this department to be under the administration of Kasetsart University on September 30, 1968, where Professor Insi Chandrasatitya took the position of the President of Kasetsart University. Institute of Food Research and Product Development (IFRPD) has officially been established since September 30, 1968. The first director of the institute was Professor Amara Bhumiratana. IFRPD has contributed as a research organization cover food related works. We assist food industries and small manufacturers by applying technology to develop their products as well as provide technical services to food industries and governmental organizations to solve food problems." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/daaa19c0-8ede-489b-802b-a5d54a14fb50> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(100.57093 13.85374)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

