<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/1937efc4-00f2-4d07-b428-160b73a8815e> <https://schema.org/description> "Founded in 1867 as the the Davenport Academy of Natural Sciences, the Putnam Museum and Science Center is a general museum housing natural science, history and anthropology collections. The natural science collections include Invertebrate &amp; Vertebrate Zoology, Botany (including the Barnes &amp; Clinton Herbaria), Geology, and Paleontology (Invertebrate, Vertebrate &amp; Paleobotany). The majority of the natural science material is derived from local sources, but the collections are worldwide in scope." .

