<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c7558d1a-9bba-4472-89ee-838747869e62> <https://schema.org/description> "The Texas A&amp;M Biodiversity Research and Teaching Collections (formerly the Texas Cooperative Wildlife Collection) is maintained by staff and faculty of the Department of Wildlife and Fisheries Sciences and is one of several natural history collections within the Texas A&amp;M system. The facility houses important collections of fishes, amphibians, reptiles, birds, mammals, parasites, and marine invertebrates that are available for use by the scientific community. Our records are searchable via VertNET and GBIF, or by contacting the curitoral staff via e-mail at brtc@tamu.edu." .

