<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/441644cf-bbad-4251-a31b-136f5125ae4c> <https://schema.org/description> "The Institute of Microbiology of the National Academy of Sciences of Belarus was organized in 1975 from the former Department of Microbiology, which had been functioning in the Belarusian Academy of Sciences since 1966. Currently, it is one of the leading research centers of Belarus in the area of microbiology and biotechnology. Its scientific activities are focused on the study of diversity, physiology and genomics of microorganisms, as well as on the development of microbial biotechnologies for agriculture, health care, industry and environmental protection. Belarus. Bacteria, Yeasts, Mycelial fungi, Bacteriophages" .
