<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/15903c25-4251-4931-ae66-365a39b70264> <https://schema.org/description> "The Royal Agricultural University (RAU) has been at the forefront of agricultural education and a key contributor to the land-based sector for 175 years. The RAU has c.1100 students studying agriculture, business, environment, equine science, farm management, food, real estate, and rural land management. The RAU is based in Cirencester, Gloucestershire, UK. The RAU's herbarium collection comprises c.10,000 specimens (c.4000 sheets). These are predominantly UK wild plants (largest proportion first - forbs, graminoids, ferns, bryophytes, lichens) with the majority dating to the 19th century. A smaller proportion are UK arable plants (arable weeds) that appear to be a teaching collection dating to the mid-19th century." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/15903c25-4251-4931-ae66-365a39b70264> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3445856> .
