<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/268a0263-0e6d-41d2-9dc9-775a91a0c899> <https://schema.org/name> "National Science and Technology Development Agency (NSTDA)" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/268a0263-0e6d-41d2-9dc9-775a91a0c899> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "BBH" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/268a0263-0e6d-41d2-9dc9-775a91a0c899> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated Jan 2013 (staff update). Formerly listed under BANGKOK; ; Description of the fungus herbarium:; The BIOTEC Fungal Herbarium was established in 1996 and was registered with Index Herbariorum in 2003. The herbarium has been housed in a purpose-built temperature/humidity controlled facility since 2003. The facility holds 40+ type specimens. Of the 20000+ specimens almost half represent insect fungi. Other major groups include Basidiomycetes (especially Marasmius and Mycena and allied genera) and Xylariales. ; ; Despcription of the plant herbarium:; The BIOTEC Plant Herbarium is managed by the Ecology and Geo-informatics Lab, and specializes in storing and distributing voucher specimens from the biodiversity research plots established by the Lab. Its main plot is the 30-ha forest dynamics plot in Khao Yai National Park. Voucher specimens from other research projects within BIOTEC and outside collaborators are also stored. Fungi of Thailand; Plant specimens from the biodiversity research plots established by the Lab for studies of ae 30-ha forest dynamics plot in Khao Yai National Park." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/268a0263-0e6d-41d2-9dc9-775a91a0c899> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(100.603982 14.080094)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

