<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/2bea4bb3-e0fa-46be-88fb-e311b23804e8> <https://schema.org/description> "HERBARIUM: The BHUPM general herbarium was founded by Johann Eduard Julius Schrader (1809-1898), who worked at Königlich-Preussische Bibliothek, today Staatsbibliothek Berlin. C. G. Ehrenberg collection (ca 1830-1870) of BHUPM contains types for several thousand species and several hundred genera. 45 000 seed collections. This is part of Museum für Naturkunde Berlin, Germany, see http://grbio.org/institution/museum-f%C3%BCr-naturkunde. Worldwide, with two main collections: 1) C. G. Ehrenberg collection of recent and fossil protists, including diatoms and other algae; 2) general collections, mainly angiosperms." .
