<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/6c6407e1-14d6-44df-b2f6-24ad95ad0585> <https://schema.org/description> "The museum is owned and run by Whitby Literary and Philosophical Society, a charity that also runs a reference library and archives. `The museum has a full range of collections from socil history to costumes to fossils and natural history. Mainly focussed around Whitby and the North York Moors villages and the Yorkshire coast geology. Also ethnographic collections from Polynesia, western Canada and the Arctc, These are NOT natural history with the exception of a narwhal skeleton." .
