<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/be33fd0d-131e-42e7-abd0-eeb003378318> <https://schema.org/description> "Located on the Baylor University campus, the Mayborn Museum Complex features a natural science and cultural history museum focusing on Central Texas, with walk-in dioramas including one on the Waco Mammoth Site, and exploration stations for geology, paleontology, archaeology, and natural history. In addition to the natural history exhibits, there are two floors of themed discovery rooms that encourage hands-on learning for all ages. Texas." .
