<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/da6c7fff-b299-4ece-8cbf-40f759e4e610> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/da6c7fff-b299-4ece-8cbf-40f759e4e610> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/da6c7fff-b299-4ece-8cbf-40f759e4e610> <https://schema.org/name> "Natural History Museum in Belgrade" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/da6c7fff-b299-4ece-8cbf-40f759e4e610> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "NHMBEO" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/da6c7fff-b299-4ece-8cbf-40f759e4e610> <https://schema.org/description> "The Natural History Museum in Belgrade (NHMB) is one of the oldest Serbian national institutions and is the only institution of its kind in Serbia; as well, it is one of the leading natural history museums in Eastern Europe because of the richness and diversity of its material. Founded in 1895 as “Jestastvenički muzej srpske zemlje”, it houses 117 natural history collections comprising about 1,500,000 specimens from Serbia, the Balkan Peninsula and the rest of the world, with a large number of them containing entomological material ([Nahirnic et al. 2012](https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Gerhard-Tarmann/publication/274736269_Nahirnic_A_Jaksic_P_Tarmann_G_M_2012_Zygaenidae_Lepidoptera_in_the_collections_of_the_Natural_History_Museum_in_Belgrade_Serbia_Bulletin_of_the_Natural_History_Museum_Belgrade_5_73-94_figs_1-3/links/552fbaed0cf27acb0de65953/Nahirnic-A-Jaksic-P-Tarmann-G-M-2012-Zygaenidae-Lepidoptera-in-the-collections-of-the-Natural-History-Museum-in-Belgrade-Serbia-Bulletin-of-the-Natural-History-Museum-Belgrade-5-73-94-figs-1-3.pdf)). The museum has a Botanical department, which holds a Herbarium (code BEO at Index Herbariorum). The musem has also [specialists](https://nhmbeo.rs/organizaciona-struktura/) in the following fields: Ichtyology, Ornithology, Mammals, Mycology, Herpetology, Entomology, Palaeozoology, Palaeobotany. At the Museum there is also an [Animal Marking Center](https://nhmbeo.rs/centar-za-markiranje-zivotinja/) that organizes the monitoring and study of animal movements at local, regional, continental and intercontinental levels. Birds are marked the most, and bats to a lesser extent. Different markers are used for marking - aluminum and plastic rings or wing stamps. For the first time in the world, birds were scientifically and planned marked in 1903, and the earliest marking of birds in the territory of today's Serbia was done only five years after that, already on June 28, 1908. The first marking of bats was carried out in 1954. See history of museum and collections here: https://scindeks-clanci.ceon.rs/data/pdf/1820-9521/2020/1820-95212013007M.pdf. Balkan Peninsula; former Yugoslavia, including Serbia, Montenegro, Slovenia, Croatia, Bosnia and Herzegovina, and FYR Macedonia; Greece; Bulgaria; Albania. fungi, plants, animals (verterbrate, invertebrate)" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/da6c7fff-b299-4ece-8cbf-40f759e4e610> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6940959> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/da6c7fff-b299-4ece-8cbf-40f759e4e610> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(20.471124 44.802406)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
