<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/deb44a4e-d83a-46d3-94d1-3d11d351740b> <https://schema.org/name> "Tullie House Museum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/deb44a4e-d83a-46d3-94d1-3d11d351740b> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "CLE" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/deb44a4e-d83a-46d3-94d1-3d11d351740b> <https://schema.org/description> "Located in Carlisle, Cumbria, in Northern England, Tullie is a regional museum supporting a designated Natural Science collection, primarily focused on the representation of local species. The collections are accessed for research fairly frequently, with a drive to become a greater, more accessible resource for the local area. The museum collections largely date from 1893 when Tullie House Museum opened, although some natural history material was transferred from a previous museum in the city. Carlisle Natural History Society was established in the same year as Tullie House and has met in the museum ever since. Tullie House Museum established what may have been the first ever local biological records centre in 1902. Today, the Museum maintains a local biological records database covering the county of Cumbria, which holds information on the distribution and abundance of wildlife in the county, of over 2,000,000 records." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/deb44a4e-d83a-46d3-94d1-3d11d351740b> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/001000g32> .
