<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e208c3eb-21b7-42cd-9ff0-0dafea1d23d1> <https://schema.org/name> "Department of Biology and Ecology, Faculty of Sciences, University of Novi Sad" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e208c3eb-21b7-42cd-9ff0-0dafea1d23d1> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "DBE-UNS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e208c3eb-21b7-42cd-9ff0-0dafea1d23d1> <https://schema.org/description> "The Department of Biology and Ecology belongs to an educational and scientific institution (Faculty of Sciences) and its main activity is to educate experts in biology (research oriented professionals, as well as secondary and elementary school teachers) and ecology. The teaching process is conducted through lectures and practical classes in amphitheatres with modern equipment, classrooms suitable for practical work and laboratories. Our Department features a rich collection of plant and animal material available to students for educational and research purposes. A compulsory part of studying biology and ecology comprises field work when students collect plant and animal material and learn how to recognize and classify it in the process of creating their own collections. Former Yugoslavia, especially Vojvodina, Serbia, Montenegro, and Balkan Peninsula. Vascular plants, fungi, insects, mollusks" .
