<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e3f78e8a-c89a-41d4-beb2-17318e8eab00> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e3f78e8a-c89a-41d4-beb2-17318e8eab00> <https://schema.org/name> "Royal Pavilion and Museums Trust" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e3f78e8a-c89a-41d4-beb2-17318e8eab00> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "BTNRP" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e3f78e8a-c89a-41d4-beb2-17318e8eab00> <https://schema.org/description> "The Booth Museum of Natural History, located in Dyke Road, Brighton, is the home of the Brighton Natural History collections. These collections include the Booth British bird dioramas, which are the first known examples ofdioramas of birds in their observed habitat. It also includes one of the largest lepidoptera collections otside of the national collections, along with good collections of Sussex geology, botany and conchology. The collection is open to researchers and artists and we encourage use by a range of academic disciplines. Worldwide, with strengths in UK, Central and , South American and Indian specimens" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e3f78e8a-c89a-41d4-beb2-17318e8eab00> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-0.153066 50.837302)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e410b89e-33c4-4d03-b707-0db173791eca> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e410b89e-33c4-4d03-b707-0db173791eca> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e410b89e-33c4-4d03-b707-0db173791eca> <https://schema.org/name> "Muséum des sciences naturelles d'Angers" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e410b89e-33c4-4d03-b707-0db173791eca> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "ANG" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/e410b89e-33c4-4d03-b707-0db173791eca> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated march 2015 (staff update). Formerly known as Herbier Lloyd or Arboretum de la Maulévrie or Musée botanique d'Angers details of names and locations : 1804-1898 : Jardin des plantes d'Angers, (F-49100 Angers) 1899-1964 : herbier Lloyd (place Imbach, F-49100 Angers) 1964 - 2005 : Musée botanique (Arboretum de la Maulévrie, 9 rue du Chateau d'Orgemont, F-49000 Angers) 2005 -present : Muséum d'Angers - herbier (Arboretum de la Maulévrie, 9 rue du Chateau d'Orgemont, F-49000 Angers). Europe, especially France." .
