<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f9bc71e2-fe10-46c8-8448-67de06bb5d7f> <https://schema.org/description> "DIATOM OF CONNECTICUT CYMBELLACEAE Cymbella janischii (A. Schmidt) De Toni USA: Connecticut: Litchfield County: Barkhamsted: Farmington River: Farmington River, Barkhamsted. West Branch of river. 41&deg;55&#39;45&quot;N, 72&deg;58&#39;22&quot;W. Accuracy: within 6-20 km Prolifically growing, musilaginous tufts, whitish gray, epilithic in no more than 35 cm. Sunny, open area. Most abundant in center of river, around small islands Khan-Bureau, Diba 17 JUL 2012 George Safford Torrey Herbarium (CONN) Department of Ecology &amp; Evolutionary Biology University of Connecticut Barcode: CONN00178538. Northeastern North America, especially Connecticut and New England; North America; New World tropics; northeastern U.S. mosses, lichens, and fungi; Tertiary angiosperms; Devonian flora; invasive species; aquatic angiosperms." .
