<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/241f1116-604b-4815-a615-5375ba9fc9ef> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/241f1116-604b-4815-a615-5375ba9fc9ef> <https://schema.org/name> "Institute of Biodiversity and Ecosystem Research, Bulgarian Academy of Sciences" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/241f1116-604b-4815-a615-5375ba9fc9ef> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "IBER-BAS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/241f1116-604b-4815-a615-5375ba9fc9ef> <https://schema.org/description> "The Institute of Biodiversity and Ecosystem Research – Bulgarian Academy of Sciences (IBER-BAS) was founded on 1 July 2010 by merging the former Institute of Zoology (base 2), Institute of Botany (base 3, founded in 1948) and Central Laboratory of General Ecology - Bulgarian Academy of Sciences (base 1). The institute carries out research in pure and applied aspects of ecology, biodiversity, nature conservation and sustainable use of biological resources. It has highly-qualified research staff. It trains PhD students in botany, mycology, zoology, enthomology, wildlife parasitology, ecology, hydrobiology, conservation biology, environmental genetics, evolutionary biology and other closely related scientific areas. It provides scientific service and methodological support to the state institutions and non-governmental structures. IBER-BAS is a member of the Consortium of European Taxonomic Facilities (CETAF). Scientific collections Currently in IBER-BAS are preserved Herbarium, Mycological, Palaeobotanical and Palynological Collections, Collection of Living Plants and Zoological Collections. In addition to these organized and catalogued collections, there are further collections, mostly parasitic worms, soil nematodes, gastropods, millipedes, aquatic invertebrates, small mammals, in a process of organisations, registration and cataloguing. Herbarium of vascular plants and bryophytes SOM (about 159 200 specimens); Mycological collection SOMF (25 600 specimens); Collection of plant fossils (about 16 000 specimens), and cuticle collection (about 2 700 species), digitised together as the same virtual collection: Paleobotanical Collection (PB) Herbarium SOM Palynological Collection (PB) - reference palynological collection (about 2 800 species) Еx situ Collection of Living Plants Protozoological Collection Helminthological Collection Nematological Collection Malacological Collection Aquatic Invertebrates Collection Millipede Collection Entomological and Arachnological Collections Fossil Mammals Collection Recent Mammals Collection. Bulgaria, Balkan Peninsula, Europe, worldwide. vascular plants, fungi, protozooloa, helminths, nematods, Gastropoda, aquatic Invertebrates, millipede, insects, spiders, fossil mammals, recent mammals" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/241f1116-604b-4815-a615-5375ba9fc9ef> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <https://ror.org/03eywck07> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/241f1116-604b-4815-a615-5375ba9fc9ef> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(23.366339 42.672451)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/241f1116-604b-4815-a615-5375ba9fc9ef> <https://schema.org/logo> <http://www.iber.bas.bg/themes/zeropoint/logo.png> .

