<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4142a8a5-c656-41f8-9080-5131df96df2a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4142a8a5-c656-41f8-9080-5131df96df2a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4142a8a5-c656-41f8-9080-5131df96df2a> <https://schema.org/name> "Scarborough College, University of Toronto" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4142a8a5-c656-41f8-9080-5131df96df2a> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "TRTS" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4142a8a5-c656-41f8-9080-5131df96df2a> <https://schema.org/description> "The University of Toronto Scarborough (UTSC) sits on 123 hectares (300 acres) of land, forming the west side of the Highland Creek neighbourhood in Scarborough. For thousands of years it has been the traditional land of the Huron-Wendat, the Seneca, and most recently, the Mississaugas of the Credit River. Today, this meeting place is still the home to many Indigenous people from across Turtle Island and we are grateful to have the opportunity to work on this land. UTSC has 14 academic departments, and approximately 13,500 undergraduate and 400 graduate students. The Department of Biological Sciences at UTSC is home to the BUGS lab ('Biodiversity of Urban Green Spaces') insect collection, which curates mainly Hymenopteran species from Ontario and Eastern Canada.Former home of the TRTS Herbarium." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4142a8a5-c656-41f8-9080-5131df96df2a> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-79.179932 43.769886)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/41930fa9-e6da-4351-bc6e-59dfaca3be7d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/41930fa9-e6da-4351-bc6e-59dfaca3be7d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/41930fa9-e6da-4351-bc6e-59dfaca3be7d> <https://schema.org/name> "UiT The Arctic University of Norway" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/41930fa9-e6da-4351-bc6e-59dfaca3be7d> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "UiT" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/41930fa9-e6da-4351-bc6e-59dfaca3be7d> <https://schema.org/description> "The University of Tromsø - The Arctic University of Norway was established 1968 and is the world’s northernmost university. In 1976, Tromsø Museum, founded 1872 as oldest scientific institution of Northern Norway, was incorporated into the University of Tromsø. Both the University of Tromsø and Tromsø Museum changed names in 2013 to “The University of Tromsø – The Arctic University of Norway” and “The Arctic University Museum of Norway”, respectively. The Norwegian name of the university is Universitetet i Tromsø – Norges arktiske universitet, which is abbreviated to UiT – Norges arktiske universitet. The Norwegian abbreviation UiT is used in the official English translation of the name.Tromsø Museum used the institution codes TROM for the herbarium and botanical collections and TSZ for the zoological collections. These institution codes are still in use at the Arctic University Museum of Norway. worldwide; Northern Norway; Spitsbergen" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/41930fa9-e6da-4351-bc6e-59dfaca3be7d> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q279724> .
