<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/4f6cfaea-ef96-489f-8ce2-9961658bc01a> <https://schema.org/description> "The National Herbarium of Cambodia was established in 2011. It is located in the Department of biology, Faculty of Science at the Royal University of Phnom Penh (RUPP). It currently has some 12 500 specimens collected in Cambodia over the 15 last years and some donated by the Muséum National d'Histoire Naturelle of Paris. The creation of the National Herbarium is a result of a strong collaboration since 1994 between the Faculty of Sciences at the Royal University of Phnom Penh and the Muséum national d'histoire naturelle of Paris. The Cambodia flora is not well known. The UNEP-World Conservation Monitoring Centre 2000 estimates over 8000 plant species, at least 10% of which could be endemic. Cambodia and southeast Asia" .
