<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5ecfdb7d-77e1-478b-946c-a2ed1091980a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5ecfdb7d-77e1-478b-946c-a2ed1091980a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5ecfdb7d-77e1-478b-946c-a2ed1091980a> <https://schema.org/name> "Craven Museum and Gallery" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5ecfdb7d-77e1-478b-946c-a2ed1091980a> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "SKIPM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5ecfdb7d-77e1-478b-946c-a2ed1091980a> <https://schema.org/description> "Craven Museum contains approximately 60,000 items mainly collected from the Craven area. It was set up by members of various local interest groups and societies, such as the Craven Naturalists and Scientific Association and the Mechanics' Institute. It is a varied, mixed collection, covering the geology and landscape of the local area, along with the history of the people who have lived here. We work with local community groups and schools to make sure our collection is accessible to all. We are also open to researchers and often work with students and staff from local instutions (such as the archaeology department at Bradford University). The museum mainly collects items from the Craven district area, which covers parts of North and West Yorkshire (as well as the Yorkshire Dales). However, some of the museum's founding collectors collected objects from further afield, including some material from the rest of the country (mainly the wider Yorkshire area) along with other countries (mostly from the African continent)." .
