<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/628ac42a-c35d-4ccf-8e66-f9eac0123748> <https://schema.org/description> "The National Museum of Bosnia and Herzegovina engages in museological, scientific, educational, and publishing activities, which determine its organisational structure. It is made up of four main departments: the Archeology Department, the Ethnology Department, the Natural Sciences Department and the Library. The National Museum of Bosnia and Herzegovina comprises some of the oldest and richest Natural History collections in the Balkans. During more than 115 years of existence and through research conducted by the scientists from the Museum, vast collections have been gathered, mostly from the Balkan Peninsula. Balkans, especially Bosnia and Herzegovina." .
