<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/72304ee8-664b-4c1d-90df-4a5b311fdfd8> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated Aug 2012. WAT is now inactive. Approximately 65,000 specimens in WAT were transferred to MT ; on 10 Aug 2012. WAT fully integrated in to MT and operated as a separate unit.; WAT Herbarium specimens should be cited as WAT. All correspondence ; relative to loans and exchanges should be with MT; African collections made by former curator John Morton are now at MO, and his North American and British Isles collections are at TRT. Vascular plants; mostly North America, especially Ontario; Asteraceae; Lamiaceae; Caryophyllaceae." .
