<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/855f37c2-ed2d-4756-996c-48915719009e> <https://schema.org/description> "The Herbarium Universitatis Senensis (SIENA) contains more than 90,000 exsiccata of vascular plants and about 9000 exsiccata of lichens, bryophytes, fungi and algae. It is organised in various sections: Historical Collection, Spermotheca, Xylotheca and Modern Collection. Mainly specimens of Tuscany, collected in the course of pure (flora, vegetation, phytogeography) and applied (environmental monitoring, biodiversity studies) research by the Department of Life Sciences, are deposited in the Modern Collections. Europe, especially Italy and Tuscany. Bryophytes, Fungi, Pteridophytes, Gymnosperms, Angiosperms" .
