<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/860a2ce6-3173-4031-82b6-55d841bdce8e> <https://schema.org/name> "Texas A&M University" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/860a2ce6-3173-4031-82b6-55d841bdce8e> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "TAMU" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/860a2ce6-3173-4031-82b6-55d841bdce8e> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated Aug 2012. TAMU is in the process of being merged with TAES. When the merger is complete, there will be no collections left at the previous location of TAMU, although the collections will maintain a separate identity after it is moved to TAES, and TAMU specimens should continue to be cited as such. The URL or TAMU is still active. An announcement will be circulated when the merger is completed. Lichen specimens previously held at TAMU are on permanent loan to OMA. Bryophytes from TAMU are now at TAES. Vascular plants of Texas; domesticated and cultivated plants; macroalgae of the Texas Gulf Coast." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/860a2ce6-3173-4031-82b6-55d841bdce8e> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-96.338956 30.614775)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8653dc83-5222-488d-b91e-5668cf232e2c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8653dc83-5222-488d-b91e-5668cf232e2c> <https://schema.org/name> "Universidade Federal de Rondônia" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8653dc83-5222-488d-b91e-5668cf232e2c> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "RON" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8653dc83-5222-488d-b91e-5668cf232e2c> <https://schema.org/description> "Entered Aug 2011. ; The collection is organized following evolutionary system, APG III. We have: 700 samples of bryophytes; 200 samples of pteridophytes; 4100 samples of angiosperms. Our mission is to be one of reference herbarium from southwest Amazonia and provide information from the Rondônia Flora. The herbarium is a member of: Nacional Institute from Science and Technology of Flora and Fungi, Brazilian Network of Herbaria, Rescue and Integration of Botanical Data for Conservation in the Southwest Amazon, and Amazonian Reflora. Most of the collection comes from the area of impact of the Santo Antonio and Jirau Hydroelectric, that are in construction on Madeira River. We also have in our collections, plants from the Plan of Agriculture and Forests of Rondônia (PLANAFLORO), made in 1996." .
