<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8eacb70a-f276-4a2c-aaa6-fb7a5bc60138> <https://schema.org/description> "Entered Dec 2009. The Herbarium of IBSS is the biggest Ukrainian collection of macrophytes of the world's oceans. The herbarium is part of the Sevastopol Biological Statiion (founded in 1872). The first collection was destroyed by fire during Second World War (1941). Current herbarium specimens of macroalgae and seagrasses date mostly from 1914 to 1992. The herbarium contains 540 species algae and seagrasses from Indian, Atlantic and Pacific Oceans. Half of specimens represent the Black Sea flora of macroalgae." .
