<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/adbcf6bb-4718-4f96-bd4f-cad7116f0d60> <https://schema.org/description> "The UTEP Biodiversity Collections include natural history specimens of animals, plants, and fossils. The collections are housed in the Biology building, which is part of the university's department of Biological Sciences. The UTEP Biodiversity Collections have a MOU with the UTEP Centennial Museum and Chihuahuan Desert Gardens. Desert mountain ranges of southern New Mexico and western Texas; Chihuahua and Durango; tropical America; southeastern Asia." .
