<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c2f063fa-6056-4387-9177-354b735e3561> <https://schema.org/name> "Holmesdale Natural History Club Museum" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c2f063fa-6056-4387-9177-354b735e3561> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "RTE" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c2f063fa-6056-4387-9177-354b735e3561> <https://schema.org/description> "The Holmesdale Natural History Club was founded in 1857 and is a member's club. From the earliest days members would donate specimens to the Club and since 1910 we have been based at our own private museum in Reigate. Collections cover Natural History - with herbarium specimens dating back to the 18th Century with the majority dating to the mid 19th Century. We also have extensive collections of insects - mainly butterflies, moths and beetles, taxidermy - mainly birds and other natural history specimens. We also have a large collection of minerals and fossils as well as many miscellaneous items. The Museum also holds collections or archaeology and local history as well as bygones and curios. England" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c2f063fa-6056-4387-9177-354b735e3561> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-0.203958 51.235027)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

