<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/c998b975-6b11-41c2-87ca-f7f2fa53741c> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated Jun 2009. Quoted from the TROY website: \"The Troy University Herbarium (TROY) was established in 1954 by Dr. Robert Dietz, who served as curator of the collection until 1986. In 1961, the herbarium was moved from Bibb Graves Hall into room 116 of the new science building, McCall Hall. It remained in that location until 1987 when it was closed and all of the specimens, approximately 1000, were destroyed. In 1997, the TROY Herbarium was reestablished by Dr. Michael Woods and Dr. Alvin Diamond in. Alabama." .
