<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/73c61524-b2fe-461c-bc91-aaa47a30a15b> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "PERGM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/73c61524-b2fe-461c-bc91-aaa47a30a15b> <https://schema.org/description> "Perth Museum and Art Gallery is one of the oldest museums in the United Kingdom. The oldest part of the building dates from 1822 and was originally the museum of the Literary & Antiquarian Society of Perth, founded in 1784. The majority of the present day Museum & Art Gallery was opened in 1935. It incorporates the collections of natural history made by the Perthshire Society of Natural Science during the late nineteenth century; this collection was originally on display in the Society’s museum on Tay Street in Perth. When that museum closed in 1902 the collections were gifted to Perth Town Council and later displayed in the new Perth Museum & Art Gallery., Perth Museum & Art Gallery provides all the services of a modern regional museum service – a high standard of collections care, learning and access, research, information and enquiries. This includes permanent exhibits and a changing programme of temporary exhibitions and special events. Professional and committed staff deliver high quality public serv.. All regions of the world." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/73c61524-b2fe-461c-bc91-aaa47a30a15b> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-3.427596 56.398136)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .

