<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/74c59534-f2e1-4c88-ade6-4b957b895225> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/74c59534-f2e1-4c88-ade6-4b957b895225> <https://schema.org/name> "Ali Nihat Gokyigit Foundation Nezahat Gokyigit Botanic Garden" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/74c59534-f2e1-4c88-ade6-4b957b895225> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "NGBB" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/74c59534-f2e1-4c88-ade6-4b957b895225> <https://schema.org/description> "The Nezahat Gökyiğit Botanical Garden (NGBG) was established in 1995 by Ali Nihat Gökyiğit as a memorial park in honour of his wife, Nezahat Gökyiğit. Its purpose was later changed, and in 2003, its name was changed to the Nezahat Gökyiğit Botanical Garden. The NGBB Herbarium was established in 2004 and currently holds approximately 20,000 plant specimens. As of 2022, data on the herbarium specimens has been transferred to the web environment, and our virtual herbarium has begun to provide services. This process is still ongoing." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/74c59534-f2e1-4c88-ade6-4b957b895225> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(29.118674 40.995359)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
