<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/80226a87-d07b-4f3c-bc18-02e496130f01> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/80226a87-d07b-4f3c-bc18-02e496130f01> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/CollegeOrUniversity> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/80226a87-d07b-4f3c-bc18-02e496130f01> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Museum> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/80226a87-d07b-4f3c-bc18-02e496130f01> <https://schema.org/name> "Marine Science Institute, University of the Philippines" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/80226a87-d07b-4f3c-bc18-02e496130f01> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "UPMSI" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/80226a87-d07b-4f3c-bc18-02e496130f01> <https://schema.org/description> "The UP Marine Science Institute (UP MSI) is one of seven academic institutions of the University of the Philippines’ College of Science. It is housed in its own building complex within the UP Diliman Campus in Quezon City. UP MSI was originally established as the Marine Sciences Center with the approval of its charter by the Board of Regents on 28 March 1974. At present, it pursues research, teaching, and extension work in marine biology, marine chemistry, physical oceanography, marine geology, and other related disciplines. UP MSI has diligently maintained reference collections showcasing the country’s rich marine heritage. This is now expanded into a research museum, the Marine Biodiversity Resources and Information System (MBRIS) dedicated to understanding, conserving, and managing Philippine marine biodiversity. MBRIS houses multiple marine scientific collections and laboratories to support biodiversity research." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/80226a87-d07b-4f3c-bc18-02e496130f01> <https://schema.org/sameAs> <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6764215> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/80226a87-d07b-4f3c-bc18-02e496130f01> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(121.068979 14.650776)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/80226a87-d07b-4f3c-bc18-02e496130f01> <https://schema.org/logo> <https://msi.upd.edu.ph/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/UPMSI-1.png> .

<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8069bdd4-e6f7-4bd5-8799-70fe8a72d705> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8069bdd4-e6f7-4bd5-8799-70fe8a72d705> <https://schema.org/name> "Herbario “Reinaldo Espinosa” de la Universidad Nacional de Loja" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8069bdd4-e6f7-4bd5-8799-70fe8a72d705> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "LOJA" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8069bdd4-e6f7-4bd5-8799-70fe8a72d705> <https://schema.org/description> "El Herbario ”Reinaldo Espinosa” fue fundado en 1946, conocido internacionalmente con el acrónimo LOJA, según el Index Herbariorum, constituye un centro de enseñanza e investigación de la flora de la Región Sur del País. Es una sección donde se archivan colecciones de vegetales secos, ordenados de acuerdo a un sistema de clasificación taxonómica, actualmente bajo el Sistema de Clasificación APG IV (Grupo de la Filogenia de las Angiospermas, versión 4). Está destinado a estudios científicos y comparativos de identificación taxonómica. Sirve como biblioteca y muestrario botánico representativo de la Flora de la región sur del Ecuador, para estudios comparativos, identificación de nuevas colecciones y como material didáctico y de consulta para diferentes estudios científicos a estudiantes, OGs y ONGs, locales, nacionales e internacionales. El Herbario LOJA posee 50 000 especímenes botánicos, principalmente de las provincias de Loja, Zamora Chinchipe y El Oro, por esta razón es un herbario regional. Prioriza colecciones botánicas de las tres provincias; además, cuenta con especímenes botánicos procedentes de las provincias de Morona Santiago, Napo, Pichincha y Sucumbíos que han llegado por donación. Ecuador, especially Loja, El Oro and Zamora-Chinchipe provinces; Ecuadorian medicinal plants." .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8069bdd4-e6f7-4bd5-8799-70fe8a72d705> <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/P625> "POINT(-79.19671 -3.9872)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/8069bdd4-e6f7-4bd5-8799-70fe8a72d705> <https://schema.org/logo> <http://patrimonio.ambiente.gob.ec/iptmae/logo.do?r=hebario_loja1> .

