<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/df27e63f-82b2-464e-9286-a96163c961c9> <https://schema.org/description> "Updated Jan 2013. MW is the second largest herbarium of Russia with 10,000+ additional accessions annually.; Loans and exchange are temporarily suspended. Historic collections of G. F. Hoffmann, J. F. Ehrhart, C. B. Trinius, I. Forster, and Herbarium Alchemillarum of V. N. Tikhomirov are stored separately. Specialty: Worldwide vascular plants (including 4 500 types), but strong in former U.S.S.R., especially European part (334 310 specimens), Caucasus (93 470 specimens), Crimea (30 690 specimens), Siberia and Russian Far East (152 250 specimens), and Central Asia and Kazakhstan (91 280 specimens); Mongolia (27 200 specimens); western and central Europe (39 790 specimens); other Asian countries (19 830 specimens); Eurasian bryophytes, but strong in Russia (55 190 specimens)." .
