<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/ee1fe2cc-fd6e-4bf6-a691-46518d806154> <https://schema.org/description> "https://www.gbif.org/grscicoll/institution/ee1fe2cc-fd6e-4bf6-a691-46518d806154 The Herbarium of the University of Neuchatel, Switzerland, holds collections of plants and fungi from throughout the world, but notably from the Jura mountains of Switzerland.Estimated number of specimens: 650’000 specimens; Fungi 130’000, Lichens 15’000, Bryophytes 40’000, Pteridophytes 5’000, and Gymnosperms 1’000. The flowering plants are divided into a Swiss Herbarium of 109’000 specimens, and General Herbarium of 350’000 specimens. Worldwide, but especially the Jura mountains of Switzerland. All groups. Fungi, lichens, bryophytes, pteridophytes, gymnosperms, and flowering plants." .
