<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f7d4f646-cdf8-476c-9a07-d7edcf7693e5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f7d4f646-cdf8-476c-9a07-d7edcf7693e5> <https://schema.org/name> "Université de Montréal Biodiversity Centre" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f7d4f646-cdf8-476c-9a07-d7edcf7693e5> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "UdeM" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f7d4f646-cdf8-476c-9a07-d7edcf7693e5> <https://schema.org/description> "Located on the site of the Montréal Botanical Garden, the Biodiversity Centre is a world-class centre of excellence in the field of biodiversity. It has multiple vocations: enable the long-term conservation and computerization of important collections of plants, insects and fungi ; develop innovative research programs and train a new generation of scientists in disciplines associated with inventorying biodiversity ; coordinate uploading of major biological collections databases housed on the Canadensys network’s portal, and ensure international access ; increase public awareness of the importance of inventorying and preserving biodiversity The Centre is also supported in its mission by the presence of the Secretariat of the UN Convention on Biological Diversity established in Montreal since 1996. Worldwide, especially Québec, Newfoundland, and Cuba; bryophytes of Québec. The herbarium contains 628,664 vascular plants and 50,000 bryophytes." .
