<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f9fd1a64-464a-4cbf-8a6c-60d7ca4e4446> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f9fd1a64-464a-4cbf-8a6c-60d7ca4e4446> <https://schema.org/name> "Universidad de Málaga" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f9fd1a64-464a-4cbf-8a6c-60d7ca4e4446> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "MGC" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/f9fd1a64-464a-4cbf-8a6c-60d7ca4e4446> <https://schema.org/description> "The MGC Herbarium is part of the University of Málaga and belongs to the Central Research Support Services (SCAI), within the Life Sciences Area. Its main purposes are to support research, teaching, technical training, and participation in national and international networks. The herbarium occupies a 52 m² room located on the ground floor of the Faculty of Sciences (Biology module), equipped with 14 compact cabinets (24 shelves) with a capacity of 2,300 boxes and up to 120,000 sheets. It also has an associated laboratory and office space at the SCAI facilities for fieldwork preparation, data entry, and collection management tasks. The herbarium staff consists of a single curator responsible for the maintenance, preservation, and management of the collections and databases. For specimen imaging, MGC is equipped with an EPSON 11000XL large-format scanner mounted in an inverted position to ensure specimen integrity, and a photographic studio with a light box, stand, and a Sony Alpha 6400 camera. Alternative website: https://www.scai.uma.es/areas/ccvi/her/her.html Updated October 2025." .
