<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/45fdee73-1717-4ade-a868-5ee8bdc7c81f> <https://schema.org/description> "Entered Jul 2009. The Sweeney Granite Mountains Desert Research Center Herbarium is used primarily as a teaching herbarium for visiting researchers and classes. This facility is a part of the University of California's Natural Reserve System, which serves a mission of promoting a better understanding and wise management of arid lands, especially the California deserts. Our collection is completely databased (Filemaker Pro) and available upon request; all California specimens contributed to the Consortium of California Herbaria database (http://ucjeps.berkeley.edu/consortium/). Mojave, Great Basin, and Sonoran Deserts with the primary focus on the east Mojave Desert of California." .
