<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5d15d105-c5d2-49f2-b160-2ed14874146f> <https://schema.org/alternateName> "HUP" .
<https://scientific-collections.gbif.org/institution/5d15d105-c5d2-49f2-b160-2ed14874146f> <https://schema.org/description> "updated Jan 2013 (staff, contact info update) . The herbarium of Hazara University is located near the junction of three world-famous mountain ranges: Hindukush, Himalaya and Karakorum. This area, spread over thousands of kilometers, has an altitudinal gradient raanging from 400m to world's tallest peaks including K2 (8611m), Nanga Parbat (8126m), Rakaposhi (7788m) and Tirich Mir (7690m)]. The area is famous for the Indus Valley, the rich cultural diversity of people and a great variety of biodiversity resources including diverse endemic flora, yet to be explored for its potential.; ; Herbarium Hazara University aims to document and resolve of related issues like threats of extinction to the endemic flora, extensive deforestation, habitat destruction, unmanaged grazing and urbanization etc.; ; Due to rich vegetation of its vicinity, Herbarium Hazara University can exchange enormous number of higher vascular plants and archegoniates of Western Himalaya throughout the world. Higher vascular plants and archegoniates of Western Himalaya." .
